var e={Basics:`Dasar-dasar`,"Where to begin: what makes a circuit, what conducts, how volts, amps and ohms fit together, the kinds of circuit, DC and AC — then how to use a breadboard and a multimeter.":`Tempat memulai: apa yang membentuk rangkaian, apa yang menghantarkan listrik, bagaimana volt, ampere, dan ohm saling terkait, jenis-jenis rangkaian, arus searah dan bolak-balik — lalu cara memakai breadboard dan multimeter.`,Resistors:`Resistor`,"Control how much current flows: six experiments with a handful of resistors, built with big picture-book parts or on a breadboard.":`Atur seberapa banyak arus yang mengalir: enam percobaan dengan beberapa resistor, dirakit dengan komponen besar ala buku bergambar atau di breadboard.`,"LEDs & diodes":`LED dan dioda`,"Light that only flows one way: polarity, forward voltage, why LEDs need a resistor, and the plain diode.":`Cahaya yang hanya mengalir satu arah: polaritas, tegangan maju, mengapa LED butuh resistor, dan dioda biasa.`,Capacitors:`Kapasitor`,"Store charge and let it go again: a water tank to picture it, filling up, holding on, emptying, in series and parallel, smoothing, a timer, and reading their values.":`Menyimpan muatan lalu melepaskannya lagi: tangki air untuk membayangkannya, mengisi, menahan, mengosongkan, seri dan paralel, perataan, pewaktu, dan membaca nilainya.`,"Switches & buttons":`Sakelar dan tombol`,"Open and close a circuit: push buttons, slide switches, switches that choose, AND and OR, and a light you can switch from two places.":`Membuka dan menutup rangkaian: tombol tekan, sakelar geser, sakelar pemilih, AND dan OR, serta lampu yang bisa dinyalakan dari dua tempat.`,Transistors:`Transistor`,"A small current controlling a big one: control, switching, gain, NPN and PNP, a touch switch that works through your finger, and turning a signal round.":`Arus kecil yang mengendalikan arus besar: pengendalian, pensakelaran, penguatan, NPN dan PNP, sakelar sentuh yang bekerja lewat jarimu, dan membalik sinyal.`,Sensors:`Sensor`,"Parts that react to the world: light, temperature and magnets — a night light and a heat alarm that switch themselves on, set to the point you choose.":`Komponen yang bereaksi terhadap dunia: cahaya, suhu, dan magnet — lampu tidur dan alarm panas yang menyala sendiri, pada titik yang kamu pilih.`,"Open and closed circuits":`Rangkaian terbuka dan tertutup`,"{0}. Open &<br />closed":`{0}. Terbuka &<br />tertutup`,"Current needs a loop":`Arus butuh lingkaran`,"Electricity only flows round a complete loop: out of the battery’s +, through the bulb and back into its −. Open the switch and the loop is broken — everything stops, wherever the gap is.":`Listrik hanya mengalir dalam lingkaran yang utuh: keluar dari kutub + baterai, melewati bohlam, lalu kembali ke kutub −. Buka sakelar dan lingkarannya terputus — semuanya berhenti, di mana pun celahnya.`,"Out of +, round the loop, back into −":`Keluar dari +, mengitari lingkaran, kembali ke −`,"Click the switch to open or close it":`Klik sakelar untuk membuka atau menutupnya`,"A gap anywhere stops the current everywhere":`Celah di mana saja menghentikan arus di mana-mana`,Battery:`Baterai`,"Current leaves its +<br />and comes back to −.":`Arus keluar dari +<br />dan kembali ke −.`,Switch:`Sakelar`,"Click it to open<br />or close the gap.":`Klik untuk membuka<br />atau menutup celah.`,Bulb:`Bohlam`,"Lights only while<br />the loop is closed.":`Menyala hanya saat<br />lingkaran tertutup.`,"Switch closed":`Sakelar tertutup`,"Round a closed loop the battery’s {0} pushes a current through the bulb:":`Dalam lingkaran tertutup, {0} dari baterai mendorong arus melewati bohlam:`,"The switch is closed, so that current flows — the same current in every part of the loop.":`Sakelar tertutup, jadi arus itu mengalir — arus yang sama di setiap bagian lingkaran.`,"By convention current is drawn flowing out of + and back into −. The electrons that actually carry it through the wire drift the other way, from − to +; the convention is older than the discovery of the electron.":`Menurut kesepakatan, arus digambar keluar dari + dan kembali ke −. Elektron yang sebenarnya membawanya di dalam kabel bergerak ke arah sebaliknya, dari − ke +; kesepakatan ini lebih tua daripada penemuan elektron.`,"Every light switch in your home is a gap like this one, opened and closed.":`Setiap sakelar lampu di rumahmu adalah celah seperti ini, yang dibuka dan ditutup.`,bulb:`bohlam`,closed:`tertutup`,"Light bulb":`Bohlam`,"Knife switch":`Sakelar pisau`,Wires:`Kabel`,off:`mati`,"With the switch open, the gap is an <i>open circuit</i>: its resistance is, as near as makes no difference, infinite, so I = V ÷ ∞ = {0}. Nothing flows anywhere in the loop, not just at the gap.":`Saat sakelar terbuka, celahnya adalah <i>rangkaian terbuka</i>: hambatannya praktis tak terhingga, jadi I = V ÷ ∞ = {0}. Tidak ada yang mengalir di bagian mana pun dari lingkaran, bukan hanya di celahnya.`,open:`terbuka`,"Conductors & insulators":`Konduktor dan isolator`,"{0}. Conductors &<br />insulators":`{0}. Konduktor &<br />isolator`,"What lets current through?":`Apa yang bisa dilewati arus?`,"Some materials let current flow easily — conductors, like metals. Others hardly let any through at all — insulators, like dry wood, plastic and rubber. Lay each across the gap and the bulb tells you which is which.":`Beberapa bahan mudah dilewati arus — konduktor, seperti logam. Bahan lain hampir tidak bisa dilewati sama sekali — isolator, seperti kayu kering, plastik, dan karet. Letakkan masing-masing di atas celah dan bohlam akan menunjukkan mana yang mana.`,"Metals conduct: that’s why wires are copper":`Logam menghantarkan: itulah sebabnya kabel terbuat dari tembaga`,"Dry wood and rubber insulate: no light":`Kayu kering dan karet menyekat: tidak ada cahaya`,"Graphite conducts, but resists a little":`Grafit menghantarkan, tapi sedikit menghambat`,"Across the Gap":`Di atas celah`,"Click it to try<br />another material.":`Klik untuk mencoba<br />bahan lain.`,Contacts:`Kontak`,"Two bare posts:<br />the gap to bridge.":`Dua kutub terbuka:<br />celah yang harus dijembatani.`,"Lights when the<br />material conducts.":`Menyala jika<br />bahannya menghantarkan.`,"Across the contacts":`Di atas kontak`,Copper:`Tembaga`,"A conductor: the bulb is as bright as with a plain wire.":`Konduktor: bohlam menyala seterang dengan kabel biasa.`,"Paper clip":`Klip kertas`,"Steel conducts too: no difference you could see.":`Baja juga menghantarkan: tidak ada perbedaan yang terlihat.`,"Pencil lead":`Isi pensil`,"Graphite (carbon) conducts, but resists far more than metal: the bulb dims.":`Grafit (karbon) menghantarkan, tapi jauh lebih menghambat daripada logam: bohlam meredup.`,Wood:`Kayu`,"Dry wood is an insulator: practically no current, no light.":`Kayu kering adalah isolator: hampir tidak ada arus, tidak ada cahaya.`,Rubber:`Karet`,"An insulator: practically no current, no light.":`Isolator: hampir tidak ada arus, tidak ada cahaya.`,"The material is one more resistance in the loop, after the bulb’s {0}:":`Bahan itu menjadi satu hambatan lagi dalam lingkaran, setelah {0} dari bohlam:`,"Across the gap":`Di atas celah`,Resistance:`Hambatan`,Current:`Arus`,"over {0}":`lebih dari {0}`,"practically {0}":`praktis {0}`,"The values are for a piece a few centimetres long. The pencil lead is a thin {0} one; its resistance depends on the lead, but it is always far more than a metal’s.":`Nilainya untuk potongan sepanjang beberapa sentimeter. Isi pensilnya tipis, {0}; hambatannya bergantung pada isinya, tapi selalu jauh lebih besar daripada logam.`,"Metals conduct because some of their electrons are free to move from atom to atom. In an insulator the electrons are held tightly to their atoms, so almost none can move.":`Logam menghantarkan karena sebagian elektronnya bebas berpindah dari atom ke atom. Dalam isolator, elektron terikat erat pada atomnya, jadi hampir tidak ada yang bisa bergerak.`,"two bare posts on a stand":`dua kutub terbuka pada dudukan`,"Across them":`Di atasnya`,"no current":`tidak ada arus`,"I = {0} ÷ ({1} + over {2}) = <b>practically {3}</b>":`I = {0} ÷ ({1} + lebih dari {2}) = <b>praktis {3}</b>`,"Less than three billionths of an amp: millions of times too little for the bulb to glow, and too little for most meters to show.":`Kurang dari tiga per miliar ampere: jutaan kali terlalu kecil untuk menyalakan bohlam, dan terlalu kecil untuk ditampilkan kebanyakan alat ukur.`,"Volts, amps & ohms":`Volt, ampere, dan ohm`,"{0}. Volts, amps<br />& ohms":`{0}. Volt, ampere<br />& ohm`,"Volt, Amp and Ohm":`Volt, Amp, dan Ohm`,"Think of a wire as a pipe. Volt pushes: the voltage. Amp is what gets through: the current. Ohm squeezes the pipe: the resistance. Push harder and more gets through; squeeze tighter and less does — that is Ohm’s law.":`Bayangkan kabel sebagai pipa. Volt mendorong: tegangan. Amp adalah yang lewat: arus. Ohm menjepit pipa: hambatan. Dorong lebih kuat dan lebih banyak yang lewat; jepit lebih erat dan lebih sedikit yang lewat — itulah hukum Ohm.`,"Volt (V): the push":`Volt (V): dorongan`,"Amp (A): how much gets through":`Amp (A): seberapa banyak yang lewat`,"Ohm (Ω): the squeeze that holds it back":`Ohm (Ω): jepitan yang menahan`,Volt:`Volt`,"The push.":`Dorongan.`,Amp:`Amp`,"What gets through.":`Yang lewat.`,Ohm:`Ohm`,"The squeeze.":`Jepitan.`,"How hard Volt pushes":`Seberapa kuat Volt mendorong`,"A gentle push.":`Dorongan lembut.`,"Twice the push.":`Dua kali dorongan.`,"Three times the push.":`Tiga kali dorongan.`,"How tight Ohm squeezes":`Seberapa erat Ohm menjepit`,"At {0}: {1} gets through.":`Pada {0}: {1} yang lewat.`,"Ohm’s law: the current is the voltage divided by the resistance.":`Hukum Ohm: arus adalah tegangan dibagi hambatan.`,"Volt pushes":`Volt mendorong`,"Through {0}":`Yang lewat {0}`,"It works the other ways round too: V = I × R, and R = V ÷ I.":`Berlaku juga sebaliknya: V = I × R, dan R = V ÷ I.`,"Volts are named after Alessandro Volta, amps after André-Marie Ampère and ohms after Georg Ohm.":`Volt dinamai dari Alessandro Volta, ampere dari André-Marie Ampère, dan ohm dari Georg Ohm.`,"pushing {0}":`mendorong {0}`,"squeezing {0}":`menjepit {0}`,"Types of circuit":`Jenis rangkaian`,"{0}. Types of<br />circuit":`{0}. Jenis<br />rangkaian`,"Six kinds of circuit":`Enam jenis rangkaian`,"Open or closed, shorted, in series, in parallel or a mix: the same battery and bulbs behave very differently depending on how they are wired. Pick a type and watch where the current goes.":`Terbuka atau tertutup, hubung singkat, seri, paralel, atau campuran: baterai dan bohlam yang sama berperilaku sangat berbeda tergantung cara merangkainya. Pilih satu jenis dan lihat ke mana arus mengalir.`,"Open and closed: a gap, or none":`Terbuka dan tertutup: ada celah, atau tidak`,"Series: one path, the same current through all":`Seri: satu jalur, arus yang sama melewati semuanya`,"Parallel: a path each, each fully lit":`Paralel: masing-masing punya jalur, semua menyala penuh`,"The same {0}<br />every time.":`{0} yang sama<br />setiap kali.`,"How bright shows<br />how much current.":`Terangnya menunjukkan<br />seberapa besar arus.`,Circuit:`Rangkaian`,Open:`Terbuka`,"The switch leaves a gap: the circuit is incomplete, so no current flows.":`Sakelar meninggalkan celah: rangkaian tidak lengkap, jadi tidak ada arus yang mengalir.`,Closed:`Tertutup`,"The circuit is complete: current flows and the bulb lights.":`Rangkaian lengkap: arus mengalir dan bohlam menyala.`,Short:`Hubung singkat`,"A bare wire straight across the battery: nearly all the current takes that easy path, the bulb stays dark and the battery heats up.":`Kabel telanjang langsung di atas baterai: hampir semua arus memilih jalur mudah itu, bohlam tetap padam, dan baterai memanas.`,Series:`Seri`,"One path through both bulbs: the same current flows through each, and both are dim.":`Satu jalur melewati kedua bohlam: arus yang sama melewati masing-masing, dan keduanya redup.`,Parallel:`Paralel`,"A separate path for each bulb: each gets the full {0} and shines as brightly as one on its own.":`Jalur terpisah untuk setiap bohlam: masing-masing mendapat {0} penuh dan menyala seterang satu bohlam saja.`,Combination:`Campuran`,"A mix: one bulb in series with a parallel pair.":`Campuran: satu bohlam seri dengan sepasang bohlam paralel.`,"A {0} battery and {1} bulbs (taken as a fixed {2}).":`Baterai {0} dan bohlam {1} (dianggap tetap {2}).`,"Light bulbs":`Bohlam`,"{0} · {1} each":`{0} · masing-masing {1}`,"The switch leaves a gap. With no complete path there is no current anywhere in the circuit:":`Sakelar meninggalkan celah. Tanpa jalur yang lengkap, tidak ada arus di bagian mana pun dari rangkaian:`,"So far the battery has been treated as perfect. A real one has a little resistance inside it — about {0} here — small enough to leave out next to a {1} bulb, but in a short it is nearly all that holds the current back. The bare wire ({2}) and the bulb ({3}) are side by side; together they make {4} × {5} ÷ ({6} + {7}) = {8}, just under the wire alone:":`Sejauh ini baterai dianggap sempurna. Baterai sungguhan punya sedikit hambatan di dalamnya — sekitar {0} di sini —, cukup kecil untuk diabaikan di samping bohlam {1}, tapi saat hubung singkat, hampir hanya itu yang menahan arus. Kabel telanjang ({2}) dan bohlam ({3}) bersebelahan; bersama-sama menjadi {4} × {5} ÷ ({6} + {7}) = {8}, sedikit di bawah kabel saja:`,"That leaves only {0} across the bulb, so it gets just {1} — under {2} of its power, far too little to glow. Nearly all the current goes through the wire, and the battery heats up and drains fast.":`Itu hanya menyisakan {0} pada bohlam, jadi bohlam hanya mendapat {1} — kurang dari {2} dayanya, terlalu kecil untuk menyala. Hampir semua arus lewat kabel, dan baterai memanas lalu cepat habis.`,"Don’t try this one for real: a shorted battery can get hot enough to burn you, and a lithium one can catch fire.":`Jangan coba yang ini sungguhan: baterai yang dihubung singkat bisa cukup panas untuk membakarmu, dan baterai litium bisa terbakar.`,"short!":`hubung singkat!`,"Bare wire":`Kabel telanjang`,"straight across the battery":`langsung di atas baterai`,"In series the resistances add, and the same current flows through both bulbs:":`Dalam rangkaian seri, hambatan dijumlahkan, dan arus yang sama melewati kedua bohlam:`,"Each bulb gets {0}: half the current, a quarter of the power of a bulb on its own — and a filament gives out much less than a quarter of its light when it runs that much cooler, so both are dim.":`Setiap bohlam mendapat {0}: setengah arusnya, seperempat daya bohlam yang sendirian — dan filamen memberi jauh kurang dari seperempat cahayanya saat bekerja sedingin itu, jadi keduanya redup.`,"Side by side, each bulb has the full {0} across it, so each takes what a single bulb would:":`Bersebelahan, setiap bohlam mendapat {0} penuh, jadi masing-masing mengambil arus sebanyak bohlam yang sendirian:`,"I = {0} ÷ {1} = <b>{2}</b> each, <b>{3}</b> from the battery":`I = {0} ÷ {1} = <b>{2}</b> masing-masing, <b>{3}</b> dari baterai`,"Both shine fully — and the battery has to supply twice the current.":`Keduanya menyala penuh — dan baterai harus memberi dua kali arus.`,"The parallel pair (two {0} side by side) acts like {1}, in series with the first bulb:":`Pasangan paralel (dua bohlam {0} bersebelahan) bertindak seperti {1}, seri dengan bohlam pertama:`,"All of it goes through the first bulb ({0} across it); it then splits, {1} through each of the pair ({2} across them). The first bulb is fairly bright, the pair only glow dimly.":`Semua arus melewati bohlam pertama ({0} padanya); lalu terbagi, {1} melewati masing-masing bohlam pasangan ({2} padanya). Bohlam pertama cukup terang, pasangannya hanya menyala redup.`,"Batteries: series & parallel":`Baterai: seri dan paralel`,"{0}. Series &<br />parallel cells":`{0}. Baterai seri<br />& paralel`,"Batteries in series and in parallel":`Baterai seri dan paralel`,"One AA cell gives {0}. Put two end to end — in series — and their voltages add: {1}, and the bulb shines brightly. Put them side by side — in parallel — and you still get {2}, so the bulb is no brighter than with one, but each cell gives only half the current, so together they last twice as long. The clock runs an hour every second: watch the strips on the cells.":`Satu baterai AA memberi {0}. Pasang dua ujung ke ujung — seri — dan tegangannya bertambah: {1}, dan bohlam menyala terang. Pasang bersebelahan — paralel — dan kamu tetap mendapat {2}, jadi bohlam tidak lebih terang daripada dengan satu baterai, tapi setiap baterai hanya memberi setengah arus, jadi bersama-sama tahan dua kali lebih lama. Jam berjalan satu jam setiap detik: perhatikan strip pada baterai.`,"Series: the voltages add":`Seri: tegangannya bertambah`,"Parallel: the same voltage, twice as long":`Paralel: tegangan sama, dua kali lebih lama`,"An hour of use every second":`Satu jam pemakaian setiap detik`,"AA Cell":`Baterai AA`,"{0}. Click it to<br />switch on.":`{0}. Klik untuk<br />menyalakan.`,"Bright on {0},<br />dim on {1}.":`Terang pada {0},<br />redup pada {1}.`,Batteries:`Baterai`,"One cell":`Satu baterai`,"{0}: the bulb glows dimly, for about {1} hours.":`{0}: bohlam menyala redup, selama sekitar {1} jam.`,"Two in series":`Dua secara seri`,"{0}: bright, but only for about {1} hours.":`{0}: terang, tapi hanya sekitar {1} jam.`,"Two in parallel":`Dua secara paralel`,"{0}: as dim as one cell, but for about {1} hours.":`{0}: seredup satu baterai, tapi selama sekitar {1} jam.`,"Voltage across the bulb":`Tegangan pada bohlam`,"With fresh cells and the {0} bulb (I = V ÷ R):":`Dengan baterai baru dan bohlam {0} (I = V ÷ R):`,Voltage:`Tegangan`,"Bulb’s current":`Arus bohlam`,"Each cell gives":`Tiap baterai memberi`,"Lasts about":`Tahan sekitar`,"In <b>series</b> the same current flows through both cells, one after the other, and their voltages add. The bulb gets twice the voltage and twice the current — four times the power — so it is bright, but the cells run down twice as fast as one would on its own.":`Dalam <b>seri</b> arus yang sama melewati kedua baterai, satu setelah yang lain, dan tegangannya bertambah. Bohlam mendapat dua kali tegangan dan dua kali arus — empat kali daya —, jadi terang, tapi baterai habis dua kali lebih cepat daripada satu baterai saja.`,"In <b>parallel</b> the voltage stays at {0}, so the bulb takes the same current as from one cell; but the cells share it, half each, so they last twice as long. Their capacities add: {1} × {2}.":`Dalam <b>paralel</b> tegangannya tetap {0}, jadi bohlam mengambil arus yang sama seperti dari satu baterai; tapi baterai berbagi arus itu, setengah masing-masing, jadi tahan dua kali lebih lama. Kapasitasnya bertambah: {1} × {2}.`,"A cell holds about {0}: it can give {1} for an hour, or {2} for":`Satu baterai menyimpan sekitar {0}: bisa memberi {1} selama satu jam, atau {2} selama`,"{0} ÷ {1} ≈ <b>{2} hours</b>":`{0} ÷ {1} ≈ <b>{2} jam</b>`,"(It lasts a little longer than that here: as a cell runs down its voltage sags, and the bulb draws less.)":`(Di sini sedikit lebih lama: saat baterai melemah, tegangannya turun dan bohlam mengambil arus lebih sedikit.)`,"Two cells hold the same energy however they are wired: series spends it four times as fast in this bulb, for a quarter of the time. Real alkaline cells give noticeably less when worked this hard: their mAh is measured at a gentle current, and at a few hundred milliamps they can lose a quarter of it or more. And never mix a flat cell with a fresh one: in parallel, the fresh one pushes current into the flat one.":`Dua baterai menyimpan energi yang sama bagaimanapun dirangkai: secara seri energinya dihabiskan empat kali lebih cepat di bohlam ini, dalam seperempat waktu. Baterai alkalin sungguhan memberi jauh lebih sedikit saat dipaksa sekeras ini: mAh-nya diukur pada arus kecil, dan pada beberapa ratus miliampere bisa berkurang seperempat atau lebih. Dan jangan pernah mencampur baterai habis dengan yang baru: secara paralel, yang baru mendorong arus ke yang habis.`,"AA cells":`Baterai AA`,"{0} × {1}, {2} each":`{0} × {1}, masing-masing {2}`,"Torch bulb":`Bohlam senter`,"{0} · {1} left":`{0} · sisa {1}`,flat:`habis`,"AA cell":`Baterai AA`,"AC and DC":`AC dan DC`,"{0}. AC and<br />DC":`{0}. AC dan<br />DC`,"Direct and alternating current":`Arus searah dan arus bolak-balik`,"A battery gives direct current (DC): it always flows the same way. A generator — like the ones that make the mains — gives alternating current (AC): one way, then the other, over and over. Two LEDs facing opposite ways show which way it flows right now, and the graph draws it.":`Baterai memberi arus searah (DC): selalu mengalir ke arah yang sama. Generator — seperti yang menghasilkan listrik PLN — memberi arus bolak-balik (AC): ke satu arah, lalu ke arah lain, terus-menerus. Dua LED yang menghadap berlawanan menunjukkan ke mana arus mengalir saat ini, dan grafiknya menggambarnya.`,"DC flows one way; AC keeps swapping":`DC mengalir satu arah; AC terus berganti`,"Red lights one way, green the other":`Merah menyala di satu arah, hijau di arah lain`,"Slow AC down to watch it swap":`Perlambat AC untuk melihatnya berganti`,Source:`Sumber`,"A battery (DC) or<br />a generator (AC).":`Baterai (DC) atau<br />generator (AC).`,"Red LED":`LED merah`,"Lights when current<br />flows one way.":`Menyala saat arus<br />mengalir ke satu arah.`,"Green LED":`LED hijau`,"Lights when it flows<br />the other way.":`Menyala saat arus<br />mengalir ke arah lain.`,Graph:`Grafik`,"The voltage<br />over time.":`Tegangan dari<br />waktu ke waktu.`,"DC · battery":`DC · baterai`,"Direct current: always the same way.":`Arus searah: selalu ke arah yang sama.`,"AC · generator":`AC · generator`,"Alternating current: one way, then the other.":`Arus bolak-balik: ke satu arah, lalu ke arah lain.`,"AC frequency":`Frekuensi AC`,"One cycle every two seconds: slow enough to follow.":`Satu siklus setiap dua detik: cukup lambat untuk diikuti.`,"One cycle a second.":`Satu siklus per detik.`,"Two cycles a second.":`Dua siklus per detik.`,"Ten cycles a second: each LED flashes ten times a second, a visible flicker.":`Sepuluh siklus per detik: setiap LED berkedip sepuluh kali per detik, kedipan yang terlihat.`,"The mains’ frequency: each LED flashes {0} times a second, too fast to see, so both look lit.":`Frekuensi jala-jala listrik: setiap LED berkedip {0} kali per detik, terlalu cepat untuk dilihat, jadi keduanya tampak menyala.`,"Source voltage":`Tegangan sumber`,"The generator’s voltage follows a sine wave, one full cycle (+, then −) every two seconds:":`Tegangan generator mengikuti gelombang sinus, satu siklus penuh (+, lalu −) setiap dua detik:`,"One swing from + to − and back takes":`Satu ayunan dari + ke − dan kembali memakan waktu`,"While it is above about {0} (what the red LED needs) the red one lights; below about {1}, the green one. In between, near zero, neither does — so each LED lights once per cycle.":`Saat di atas sekitar {0} (yang dibutuhkan LED merah) yang merah menyala; di bawah sekitar {1}, yang hijau. Di antaranya, dekat nol, tidak ada yang menyala — jadi setiap LED menyala sekali per siklus.`,"Right now: <b>+{0}</b>, no current.":`Saat ini: <b>+{0}</b>, tidak ada arus.`,"AC voltages are usually quoted as RMS, a kind of average that gives the same heating as DC: this source’s {0} peak is about {1} RMS.":`Tegangan AC biasanya dinyatakan dalam nilai efektif (RMS), semacam rata-rata yang memberi panas sama dengan DC: puncak {0} dari sumber ini setara sekitar {1} efektif.`,"The mains in your home is AC: {0} RMS in most of the world (a peak of about {1}) at {2} cycles a second, {3} in North America at {4} — so the current changes direction {5} or {6} times a second. Chargers turn it into the DC that phones and laptops run on.":`Listrik di rumahmu adalah AC: {0} efektif di sebagian besar dunia (puncak sekitar {1}) pada {2} siklus per detik, {3} di Amerika Utara pada {4} — jadi arus berganti arah {5} atau {6} kali per detik. Pengisi daya mengubahnya menjadi DC yang dipakai ponsel dan laptop.`,"{0} pk":`{0}p`,red:`merah`,green:`hijau`,Generator:`Generator`,"AC, {0} peak, {1}":`AC, puncak {0}, {1}`,Resistor:`Resistor`,"lets current through one way":`melewatkan arus ke satu arah`,"facing the other way":`menghadap ke arah sebaliknya`,"the voltage over time":`tegangan dari waktu ke waktu`,"Right now: <b>+{0}</b>, {1} through the red LED.":`Saat ini: <b>+{0}</b>, {1} melalui LED merah.`,"Right now: <b>{0}</b>, no current.":`Saat ini: <b>{0}</b>, tidak ada arus.`,"Right now: <b>{0}</b>, {1} through the green LED.":`Saat ini: <b>{0}</b>, {1} melalui LED hijau.`,"A battery holds its voltage steady:":`Baterai menjaga tegangannya tetap:`,"V = {0}, always":`V = {0}, selalu`,"The current only ever flows one way, so only the red LED lights:":`Arus hanya mengalir ke satu arah, jadi hanya LED merah yang menyala:`,"{0} DC":`{0} DC`,"The generator’s voltage follows a sine wave, one full cycle (+, then −) each second:":`Tegangan generator mengikuti gelombang sinus, satu siklus penuh (+, lalu −) setiap detik:`,"The generator’s voltage follows a sine wave, one full cycle (+, then −) every half second:":`Tegangan generator mengikuti gelombang sinus, satu siklus penuh (+, lalu −) setiap setengah detik:`,"The generator’s voltage follows a sine wave, one full cycle (+, then −) {0} times a second:":`Tegangan generator mengikuti gelombang sinus, satu siklus penuh (+, lalu −) {0} kali per detik:`,"At this speed the current reverses too often to draw, so the moving dashes stop; the LEDs still take turns, too fast for your eye to follow.":`Pada kecepatan ini arus berbalik terlalu sering untuk digambar, jadi garis putus-putus yang bergerak berhenti; LED tetap bergantian, terlalu cepat untuk diikuti mata.`,"Using a breadboard":`Memakai breadboard`,"{0}. Using a<br />breadboard":`{0}. Memakai<br />breadboard`,"Connecting a breadboard":`Menghubungkan breadboard`,"A breadboard lets you build circuits without soldering. Inside, metal clips join its holes: each column of five holes is one clip, and each power rail is one long clip. Connect a battery to the rails, then build a path from the + rail to the − rail through your parts — and follow the current round it.":`Breadboard memungkinkan kamu merakit rangkaian tanpa menyolder. Di dalamnya, klip logam menghubungkan lubang-lubangnya: setiap kolom lima lubang adalah satu klip, dan setiap rel daya adalah satu klip panjang. Hubungkan baterai ke rel, lalu buat jalur dari rel + ke rel − melewati komponenmu — dan ikuti arusnya.`,"Red lead into the + rail, black into the −":`Kabel merah ke rel +, hitam ke −`,"Each column of five holes is one clip inside":`Setiap kolom lima lubang adalah satu klip di dalam`,"The current goes + rail → parts → − rail":`Arus mengalir rel + → komponen → rel −`,"Battery Pack":`Tempat baterai`,"Red lead +,<br />black lead −.":`Kabel merah +,<br />kabel hitam −.`,"+ Rail":`Rel +`,"One clip, {0}<br />all along it.":`Satu klip, {0}<br />di sepanjangnya.`,"− Rail":`Rel −`,LED:`LED`,"Across two columns,<br />or shorted in one.":`Di antara dua kolom,<br />atau terhubung singkat di satu kolom.`,Step:`Langkah`,"{0} · Connect the battery":`{0} · Hubungkan baterai`,"Red lead into the + rail (red line), black into the − rail (blue line). Nothing flows yet: nothing joins the rails.":`Kabel merah ke rel + (garis merah), hitam ke rel − (garis biru). Belum ada yang mengalir: tidak ada yang menghubungkan kedua rel.`,"{0} · Build a loop":`{0} · Buat lingkaran`,"A jumper from the + rail, the resistor, the LED across two columns and a jumper back to the − rail: a complete loop.":`Kabel jumper dari rel +, resistor, LED di antara dua kolom, dan kabel jumper kembali ke rel −: satu lingkaran utuh.`,"{0} · A common mistake":`{0} · Kesalahan umum`,"Both of the LED’s legs in one column: one clip joins them, so the current goes round the LED and it stays dark.":`Kedua kaki LED di satu kolom: satu klip menghubungkannya, jadi arus memutari LED dan LED tetap padam.`,View:`Tampilan`,"From above":`Dari atas`,"The holes that are joined are shaded the same colour.":`Lubang yang terhubung diberi warna yang sama.`,Inside:`Bagian dalam`,"The plastic made see-through: a metal clip under each column of five holes, and one along each rail.":`Plastiknya dibuat tembus pandang: satu klip logam di bawah setiap kolom lima lubang, dan satu di sepanjang setiap rel.`,"The pack’s two AA cells are in series: {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>. Its red lead goes into the + rail, its black lead into the − rail.":`Dua baterai AA di tempat baterai dirangkai seri: {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>. Kabel merahnya masuk ke rel +, kabel hitamnya ke rel −.`,"Switch the pack on (its slide switch, or Power) and, as each rail is one long clip, the whole + rail is at {0} and the whole − rail at {1}, all along the board — anything plugged into a rail is connected to the battery.":`Nyalakan tempat baterai (sakelar gesernya, atau Daya) dan, karena setiap rel adalah satu klip panjang, seluruh rel + bernilai {0} dan seluruh rel − bernilai {1}, di sepanjang papan — apa pun yang dicolokkan ke rel terhubung ke baterai.`,"No current flows yet: current needs a complete path from + back to −, and nothing joins the rails.":`Belum ada arus yang mengalir: arus butuh jalur lengkap dari + kembali ke −, dan tidak ada yang menghubungkan kedua rel.`,"Never join the rails with a plain wire: that is a short circuit straight across the battery.":`Jangan pernah menghubungkan kedua rel dengan kabel biasa: itu hubung singkat langsung pada baterai.`,"+ rail: {0} all along it":`Rel +: {0} di sepanjangnya`,"− rail: {0} all along it":`Rel −: {0} di sepanjangnya`,"nothing joins them yet: no current":`belum ada yang menghubungkannya: tidak ada arus`,"Battery pack":`Tempat baterai`,"{0} × AA = {1}":`{0} × AA = {1}`,Breadboard:`Breadboard`,"from above":`dari atas`,"Follow the arrows: out of the battery’s +, along the + rail, up the jumper into column {0}, through the resistor to column {1}, through the LED to column {2}, down the jumper to the − rail and back to the battery’s −.":`Ikuti panahnya: keluar dari + baterai, di sepanjang rel +, naik lewat jumper ke kolom {0}, melewati resistor ke kolom {1}, melewati LED ke kolom {2}, turun lewat jumper ke rel −, lalu kembali ke − baterai.`,"Each part bridges two different columns, so the current has to go <i>through</i> it:":`Setiap komponen menjembatani dua kolom yang berbeda, jadi arus harus mengalir <i>melewatinya</i>:`,"The gap down the middle separates a–e from f–j: a column’s top five and bottom five are two different clips. And on some long breadboards each power rail is split in the middle (look for a break in its red or blue line): join the halves with a jumper, or check with a meter on continuity.":`Celah di tengah memisahkan a–e dari f–j: lima lubang atas dan lima lubang bawah sebuah kolom adalah dua klip yang berbeda. Dan pada beberapa breadboard panjang, setiap rel daya terputus di tengah (cari celah pada garis merah atau birunya): sambungkan kedua bagian dengan jumper, atau periksa dengan multimeter pada mode kontinuitas.`,"{0}, columns {1} to {2}":`{0}, kolom {1} sampai {2}`,"legs in columns {0} and {1}":`kaki di kolom {0} dan {1}`,"Jumper wires":`Kabel jumper`,"{0}: + rail to column {1}, a column to the − rail":`{0}: rel + ke kolom {1}, satu kolom ke rel −`,"shorted: {0}":`terhubung singkat: {0}`,"Both of the LED’s legs are in column {0}, and one clip joins all five of its holes — so the LED’s legs are joined to each other. There is {1} across the LED and no current goes through it.":`Kedua kaki LED berada di kolom {0}, dan satu klip menghubungkan kelima lubangnya — jadi kaki-kaki LED terhubung satu sama lain. Tegangan pada LED {1} dan tidak ada arus yang melewatinya.`,"The current still flows, along the clip instead. The resistor now has the whole {0} across it:":`Arus tetap mengalir, tapi lewat klip. Sekarang resistor mendapat {0} penuh:`,"I = {0} ÷ {1} = <b>{2}</b> (none of it through the LED)":`I = {0} ÷ {1} = <b>{2}</b> (tidak ada yang lewat LED)`,"The fix: turn the LED so its legs go into two different columns.":`Solusinya: putar LED agar kakinya masuk ke dua kolom berbeda.`,"shorted by":`terhubung singkat oleh`,"the clip":`klip`,"both legs in column {0}":`kedua kaki di kolom {0}`,"seen from inside: its metal clips":`dilihat dari dalam: klip logamnya`,"Using a multimeter":`Memakai multimeter`,"{0}. Using a<br />multimeter":`{0}. Memakai<br />multimeter`,"How to test with a multimeter":`Cara mengukur dengan multimeter`,"A multimeter measures voltage, current and resistance, and checks continuity — but each test is set up differently: the dial picks what to measure, the red lead goes in the right socket, and the probes touch the right places. Pick a test and watch how the meter, the leads and the probes are set.":`Multimeter mengukur tegangan, arus, dan hambatan, serta memeriksa kontinuitas — tapi setiap pengukuran disiapkan dengan cara berbeda: sakelar putar memilih apa yang diukur, kabel merah masuk ke soket yang tepat, dan probe menyentuh titik yang tepat. Pilih satu pengukuran dan lihat bagaimana multimeter, kabel, dan probe diatur.`,"The dial picks what to measure":`Sakelar putar memilih apa yang diukur`,"Black lead always in COM; red in VΩmA or {0}":`Kabel hitam selalu di COM; merah di VΩmA atau {0}`,"Volts across a part; amps through the meter":`Volt di kedua ujung komponen; ampere melewati multimeter`,Multimeter:`Multimeter`,"Dial and sockets<br />set for the test.":`Sakelar putar dan soket<br />diatur untuk pengukuran.`,"Red Probe":`Probe merah`,"The + side.":`Sisi +.`,"Black Probe":`Probe hitam`,"The − side.":`Sisi −.`,Test:`Pengukuran`,"Battery · V":`Baterai · V`,"The battery’s voltage: the probes on its two ends.":`Tegangan baterai: probe di kedua kutubnya.`,"Resistor · V":`Resistor · V`,"The voltage across the resistor: one probe each side of it, with the circuit running.":`Tegangan pada resistor: satu probe di tiap sisinya, saat rangkaian bekerja.`,"Bulb · V":`Bohlam · V`,"The voltage across the bulb: one probe each side of it.":`Tegangan pada bohlam: satu probe di tiap sisinya.`,"Current · A":`Arus · A`,"The current: open the circuit and put the meter in the gap, so the current flows through it.":`Arus: buka rangkaian dan pasang multimeter di celahnya, agar arus melewatinya.`,"Resistance · Ω":`Hambatan · Ω`,"A resistance: the part taken out of the circuit, no power on it.":`Sebuah hambatan: komponen dilepas dari rangkaian, tanpa daya.`,Continuity:`Kontinuitas`,"Is it connected end to end? A beep says yes.":`Apakah tersambung dari ujung ke ujung? Bunyi bip berarti ya.`,"<b>Dial:</b> V⎓ (DC volts). <b>Leads:</b> black in COM, red in VΩmA. <b>Probes:</b> red on the battery’s +, black on its −.":`<b>Sakelar putar:</b> V⎓ (volt DC). <b>Kabel:</b> hitam di COM, merah di VΩmA. <b>Probe:</b> merah di kutub + baterai, hitam di −.`,"Touching the battery’s two ends, the meter reads the voltage between them:":`Dengan menyentuh kedua kutub baterai, multimeter membaca tegangan di antaranya:`,"A fresh AA cell actually gives a little over {0}, so a new pair often reads {1}–{2}; a flat one reads well under.":`Baterai AA baru sebenarnya memberi sedikit di atas {0}, jadi sepasang baterai baru sering terbaca {1}–{2}; yang habis jauh di bawahnya.`,"V⎓ (DC volts)":`V⎓ (volt DC)`,Leads:`Kabel`,"black in COM, red in VΩmA":`hitam di COM, merah di VΩmA`,"<b>Dial:</b> V⎓ (DC volts). <b>Leads:</b> black in COM, red in VΩmA. <b>Probes:</b> one on each side of the resistor, red on the side nearer +.":`<b>Sakelar putar:</b> V⎓ (volt DC). <b>Kabel:</b> hitam di COM, merah di VΩmA. <b>Probe:</b> satu di tiap sisi resistor, merah di sisi yang lebih dekat ke +.`,"On volts the meter goes <i>across</i> the part, alongside it. Its own resistance is about {0}, so it takes almost no current and doesn’t change the circuit. The loop is the battery, {1} and the {2} bulb, so {3} flows, and":`Untuk volt, multimeter dipasang <i>di kedua ujung</i> komponen, di sampingnya. Hambatannya sendiri sekitar {0}, jadi hampir tidak mengambil arus dan tidak mengubah rangkaian. Lingkarannya terdiri dari baterai, {1}, dan bohlam {2}, jadi mengalir {3}, dan`,"Measure the bulb too: the two add up to the battery’s {0}.":`Ukur juga bohlamnya: keduanya berjumlah {0} dari baterai.`,"<b>Dial:</b> V⎓ (DC volts). <b>Leads:</b> black in COM, red in VΩmA. <b>Probes:</b> one on each side of the bulb, red on the side nearer +.":`<b>Sakelar putar:</b> V⎓ (volt DC). <b>Kabel:</b> hitam di COM, merah di VΩmA. <b>Probe:</b> satu di tiap sisi bohlam, merah di sisi yang lebih dekat ke +.`,"With {0} across the resistor, the two add up to the battery’s {1}. (Taking the bulb as a fixed {2}; at {3} it only glows dimly.)":`Dengan {0} pada resistor, keduanya berjumlah {1} dari baterai. (Bohlam dianggap tetap {2}; pada {3} bohlam hanya menyala redup.)`,"<b>Dial:</b> {0} (current). <b>Leads:</b> black in COM, red moved to {1}. <b>Probes:</b> in the gap where a wire was taken out.":`<b>Sakelar putar:</b> {0} (arus). <b>Kabel:</b> hitam di COM, merah dipindah ke {1}. <b>Probe:</b> di celah tempat sebuah kabel dilepas.`,"Current must flow <i>through</i> the meter, so the circuit is opened — here the wire between the resistor and the bulb is taken out — and the meter goes in the gap: red probe where the current comes in, black where it goes out.":`Arus harus mengalir <i>melewati</i> multimeter, jadi rangkaiannya dibuka — di sini kabel antara resistor dan bohlam dilepas — dan multimeter dipasang di celahnya: probe merah di tempat arus masuk, hitam di tempat arus keluar.`,"The red lead moves to the <b>{0}</b> socket and the dial to {1}: start there when you don’t know how big the current is. For small currents (up to about {2}) the mA setting, with the red lead back in VΩmA, gives more digits.":`Kabel merah pindah ke soket <b>{0}</b> dan sakelar putar ke {1}: mulailah dari sana saat kamu tidak tahu seberapa besar arusnya. Untuk arus kecil (sampai sekitar {2}), posisi mA, dengan kabel merah kembali di VΩmA, memberi lebih banyak digit.`,"Set to current, the meter has almost no resistance. Never touch it across a battery or a part like that: it is a short circuit, and it can blow the meter’s fuse or worse. Move the red lead back to VΩmA when you’re done.":`Pada mode arus, multimeter hampir tidak punya hambatan. Jangan pernah menempelkannya seperti itu pada baterai atau komponen: itu hubung singkat, dan bisa memutus sekring multimeter atau lebih buruk. Kembalikan kabel merah ke VΩmA setelah selesai.`,"{0} (current)":`{0} (arus)`,"black in COM, red moved to {0}":`hitam di COM, merah dipindah ke {0}`,"<b>Dial:</b> Ω (ohms). <b>Leads:</b> black in COM, red in VΩmA. <b>Probes:</b> on the resistor’s two ends, out of the circuit.":`<b>Sakelar putar:</b> Ω (ohm). <b>Kabel:</b> hitam di COM, merah di VΩmA. <b>Probe:</b> di kedua ujung resistor, di luar rangkaian.`,"The meter sends a small current of its own through the part and works out R = V ÷ I. So the part must have no power on it — and is best taken out of the circuit, since anything still connected to it would be measured too.":`Multimeter mengalirkan arus kecilnya sendiri melewati komponen dan menghitung R = V ÷ I. Jadi komponen itu tidak boleh berdaya — dan paling baik dilepas dari rangkaian, karena apa pun yang masih terhubung dengannya ikut terukur.`,"That is the {0} resistor plus about {1} of the meter’s own leads: touch the probes together to see it. A gold band means within {2}: {3}–{4}.":`Itu resistor {0} ditambah sekitar {1} dari kabel multimeter sendiri: sentuhkan kedua probe untuk melihatnya. Gelang emas berarti dalam batas {2}: {3}–{4}.`,"{0} · out of the circuit":`{0} · di luar rangkaian`,"Ω (ohms)":`Ω (ohm)`,"<b>Dial:</b> •))) (continuity). <b>Leads:</b> black in COM, red in VΩmA. <b>Probes:</b> on the wire’s two ends.":`<b>Sakelar putar:</b> •))) (kontinuitas). <b>Kabel:</b> hitam di COM, merah di VΩmA. <b>Probe:</b> di kedua ujung kabel.`,"Continuity checks that something conducts from end to end: a wire that might be broken inside, a fuse, a switch. If the resistance between the probes is low — below about {0}–{1}, depending on the meter — it beeps.":`Kontinuitas memeriksa apakah sesuatu menghantarkan dari ujung ke ujung: kabel yang mungkin putus di dalam, sekring, sakelar. Jika hambatan di antara probe rendah — di bawah sekitar {0}–{1}, tergantung multimeternya — multimeter berbunyi bip.`,"R = <b>{0}</b> — beep":`R = <b>{0}</b> — bip`,"Like resistance, only test continuity with the power off.":`Seperti hambatan, uji kontinuitas hanya saat daya mati.`,"loose wire":`kabel lepas`,"beep: it conducts":`bip: menghantarkan`,"•))) (continuity)":`•))) (kontinuitas)`,"Loose wire":`Kabel lepas`,"being tested":`sedang diuji`,"How a resistor works":`Cara kerja resistor`,"{0}. How it<br />works":`{0}. Cara<br />kerjanya`,"What a resistor does":`Apa yang dilakukan resistor`,"A resistor makes it harder for current to flow. Put one in line with a motor and it decides how much current the motor gets — and so how fast its fan spins. Too much resistance and the motor can’t even start.":`Resistor membuat arus lebih sulit mengalir. Pasang satu secara seri dengan motor dan resistor menentukan berapa arus yang didapat motor — dan seberapa cepat kipasnya berputar. Kalau hambatannya terlalu besar, motor bahkan tidak bisa mulai berputar.`,"A steady {0} volts to work with":`Tegangan {0} volt yang stabil`,"Click the resistor to swap its value":`Klik resistor untuk mengganti nilainya`,"Less resistance, more current, a faster fan":`Hambatan lebih kecil, arus lebih besar, kipas lebih cepat`,"{0} Supply":`Catu daya {0}`,"A steady {0}.<br />Click it to switch on.":`{0} yang stabil.<br />Klik untuk menyalakan.`,"Click it to try<br />another value.":`Klik untuk mencoba<br />nilai lain.`,"Motor & Fan":`Motor & kipas`,"Spins faster with<br />more current.":`Berputar lebih cepat<br />dengan arus lebih besar.`,"Power Rails":`Rel daya`,"Each long rail is one<br />connection: + and −.":`Setiap rel panjang adalah satu<br />sambungan: + dan −.`,"Build it":`Rakit`,"Without a breadboard":`Tanpa breadboard`,"Big parts and thick wires, laid out like the circuit diagram.":`Komponen besar dan kabel tebal, ditata seperti diagram rangkaian.`,"On a breadboard":`Di breadboard`,"The same circuit as you would really build it: a power supply, a breadboard and jumper wires.":`Rangkaian yang sama seperti yang benar-benar akan kamu rakit: catu daya, breadboard, dan kabel jumper.`,"About {0}: the fan turns at {1}.":`Sekitar {0}: kipas berputar {1}.`,"About {0}: not enough to start the motor.":`Sekitar {0}: tidak cukup untuk memutar motor.`,"The resistor and the motor share the supply’s {0}. With {1} in line, the current is":`Resistor dan motor berbagi {0} dari catu daya. Dengan {1} secara seri, arusnya adalah`,"Ohm’s law gives the resistor’s share of the voltage; the motor gets the rest:":`Hukum Ohm memberi bagian tegangan resistor; motor mendapat sisanya:`,"V<sub>motor</sub> = {0} − {1} = <b>{2}</b>":`V<sub>motor</sub> = {0} − {1} = <b>{2}</b>`,"Less voltage and current for the motor, and its fan turns more slowly:":`Tegangan dan arus lebih kecil untuk motor, dan kipasnya berputar lebih lambat:`,Fan:`Kipas`,stalled:`macet`,"The current isn’t just {0} ÷ (R + the coil’s {1}): a spinning motor also works as a generator and pushes back against the battery. The faster it spins, the harder it pushes back — which is why a stalled motor draws the most current.":`Arusnya bukan hanya {0} ÷ (R + {1} dari kumparan): motor yang berputar juga bekerja sebagai generator dan mendorong balik melawan baterai. Makin cepat berputar, makin kuat dorongan baliknya — itulah sebabnya motor yang macet menarik arus paling besar.`,"A motor takes hundreds of milliamps, far more than an LED, so these resistors are small — and they get warm: this one turns P = I² × R = {0} into heat. A small ¼-watt resistor is rated for at most {1} and is best kept well under that, and with the bigger values here it would have to take up to {2}, so the circuit uses {3}-watt ones.":`Motor menarik ratusan miliampere, jauh lebih besar daripada LED, jadi resistor ini kecil — dan menjadi hangat: resistor ini mengubah P = I² × R = {0} menjadi panas. Resistor kecil ¼ watt hanya tahan paling banyak {1} dan sebaiknya dipakai jauh di bawahnya, dan dengan nilai-nilai besar di sini resistor itu harus menahan sampai {2}, jadi rangkaian ini memakai resistor {3} watt.`,motor:`motor`,"DC motor with a fan":`Motor DC dengan kipas`,"{0} hobby motor":`Motor hobi {0}`,"Power supply":`Catu daya`,"{0}, and the motor’s leads":`{0}, dan kabel motor`,"A motor takes hundreds of milliamps, far more than an LED, so these resistors are small — and they get warm: this one turns P = I² × R = {0} into heat. That is more than a small ¼-watt resistor can take, so the circuit uses {1}-watt ones.":`Motor menarik ratusan miliampere, jauh lebih besar daripada LED, jadi resistor ini kecil — dan menjadi hangat: resistor ini mengubah P = I² × R = {0} menjadi panas. Itu lebih dari yang bisa ditahan resistor kecil ¼ watt, jadi rangkaian ini memakai resistor {1} watt.`,"With {0} the motor can’t start: {1} still flows through its coil, but that is too little to overcome the friction.":`Dengan {0} motor tidak bisa mulai berputar: masih ada {1} yang melewati kumparannya, tapi terlalu kecil untuk mengatasi gesekan.`,"Read the colour code":`Membaca kode warna`,"{0}. Colour<br />code":`{0}. Kode<br />warna`,"Resistors are too small for printed numbers, so their value is painted on in coloured bands. On the usual four-band kind: two digits, then the multiplier — how many zeros follow — then the tolerance, how far the real value may be from it. Click a band to pick it up, then dip it in a paint pot.":`Resistor terlalu kecil untuk dicetak angka, jadi nilainya dicat dengan gelang berwarna. Pada jenis umum empat gelang: dua digit, lalu pengali — berapa nol yang mengikuti —, lalu toleransi, seberapa jauh nilai sebenarnya bisa menyimpang. Klik sebuah gelang untuk mengambilnya, lalu celupkan ke pot cat.`,"Click a band, then a paint pot":`Klik sebuah gelang, lalu pot cat`,"Read from the end the bands crowd towards":`Baca dari ujung tempat gelang-gelang merapat`,"Set yourself a value to make":`Tentukan nilai yang ingin dibuat`,Bands:`Gelang`,"Click one to pick<br />it up.":`Klik satu untuk<br />mengambilnya.`,"Its Value":`Nilainya`,"Digits × multiplier,<br />± its tolerance.":`Digit × pengali,<br />± toleransinya.`,"{0} bands":`{0} gelang`,"The usual kind: two digits, then the multiplier and tolerance.":`Jenis umum: dua digit, lalu pengali dan toleransi.`,"Precision resistors: three digits, then the multiplier and tolerance.":`Resistor presisi: tiga digit, lalu pengali dan toleransi.`,Challenge:`Tantangan`,"Free painting":`Mengecat bebas`,"Paint any value you like.":`Cat nilai apa pun yang kamu suka.`,"Make {0}":`Buat {0}`,"The resistor that keeps an LED safe on {0}.":`Resistor yang menjaga LED tetap aman pada {0}.`,"Two digits, {0} and {1}, then two zeros.":`Dua digit, {0} dan {1}, lalu dua nol.`,"The same digits, one more zero.":`Digit yang sama, satu nol lagi.`,"One million ohms: {0}, {1} and five zeros.":`Satu juta ohm: {0}, {1}, dan lima nol.`,Painting:`Mengecat`,"1st digit":`Digit ke-1`,"2nd digit":`Digit ke-2`,"3rd digit":`Digit ke-3`,Multiplier:`Pengali`,Tolerance:`Toleransi`,"1st band · digit":`Gelang ke-1 · digit`,"Brown · {0}":`Cokelat · {0}`,"Red · {0}":`Merah · {0}`,"Orange · {0}":`Oranye · {0}`,"Yellow · {0}":`Kuning · {0}`,"Green · {0}":`Hijau · {0}`,"Blue · {0}":`Biru · {0}`,"Violet · {0}":`Ungu · {0}`,"Grey · {0}":`Abu-abu · {0}`,"White · {0}":`Putih · {0}`,"2nd band · digit":`Gelang ke-2 · digit`,"Black · {0}":`Hitam · {0}`,"3rd band · digit":`Gelang ke-3 · digit`,"Multiplier · ×":`Pengali · ×`,"Black · × {0}":`Hitam · × {0}`,"Brown · × {0}":`Cokelat · × {0}`,"Red · × {0}":`Merah · × {0}`,"Orange · × 1k":`Oranye · × 1k`,"Yellow · × 10k":`Kuning · × 10k`,"Green · × 100k":`Hijau · × 100k`,"Blue · × 1M":`Biru · × 1M`,"Gold · × {0}":`Emas · × {0}`,"Silver · × {0}":`Perak · × {0}`,"Tolerance · ±":`Toleransi · ±`,"Brown · ±{0}":`Cokelat · ±{0}`,"Red · ±{0}":`Merah · ±{0}`,"Green · ±{0}":`Hijau · ±{0}`,"Gold · ±{0}":`Emas · ±{0}`,"Silver · ±{0}":`Perak · ±{0}`,"Read the bands from the end they crowd towards (the tolerance band stands apart at the other end):":`Baca gelang dari ujung tempat gelang-gelang merapat (gelang toleransi terpisah di ujung lainnya):`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>1st digit</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>2nd digit</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× {2}</b><small>multiplier</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{3}</b><small>tolerance</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>digit ke-1</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>digit ke-2</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× {2}</b><small>pengali</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{3}</b><small>toleransi</small></span>`,"Within ±{0}, anything from {1} to {2} is a good resistor.":`Dalam batas ±{0}, nilai berapa pun dari {1} sampai {2} adalah resistor yang baik.`,Colour:`Warna`,Digit:`Digit`,"{t0}</span> Black":`{t0}</span> Hitam`,"{t0}</span> Brown":`{t0}</span> Cokelat`,"{t0}</span> Red":`{t0}</span> Merah`,"{t0}</span> Orange":`{t0}</span> Oranye`,"{t0}</span> Yellow":`{t0}</span> Kuning`,"{t0}</span> Green":`{t0}</span> Hijau`,"{t0}</span> Blue":`{t0}</span> Biru`,"{t0}</span> Violet":`{t0}</span> Ungu`,"{t0}</span> Grey":`{t0}</span> Abu-abu`,"{t0}</span> White":`{t0}</span> Putih`,"{t0}</span> Gold":`{t0}</span> Emas`,"{t0}</span> Silver":`{t0}</span> Perak`,"The paint pots hold the bands you will meet most; the rest of the table (violet, grey and white as multipliers, the finest tolerances) turns up on precision parts.":`Pot cat berisi gelang yang paling sering kamu temui; sisa tabelnya (ungu, abu-abu, dan putih sebagai pengali, toleransi yang paling halus) muncul pada komponen presisi.`,"A way to remember the digits: black, brown, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet, grey, white — the rainbow, with dark colours below it and pale ones above. No tolerance band at all means ±{0}. Some resistors add a sixth band after the tolerance: how much the value drifts with temperature.":`Cara mengingat digitnya: hitam, cokelat, merah, oranye, kuning, hijau, biru, ungu, abu-abu, putih — pelangi, dengan warna gelap di bawahnya dan warna pucat di atasnya. Tanpa gelang toleransi sama sekali berarti ±{0}. Beberapa resistor menambahkan gelang keenam setelah toleransi: seberapa jauh nilainya bergeser karena suhu.`,"{0}: two digits, multiplier, tolerance":`{0}: dua digit, pengali, toleransi`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>1st digit</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>2nd digit</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>{2}</b><small>3rd digit</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>× {3}</b><small>multiplier</small></span><span>{t4}</span><b>±{4}</b><small>tolerance</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>digit ke-1</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>digit ke-2</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>{2}</b><small>digit ke-3</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>× {3}</b><small>pengali</small></span><span>{t4}</span><b>±{4}</b><small>toleransi</small></span>`,"{0}: three digits, multiplier, tolerance":`{0}: tiga digit, pengali, toleransi`,"The challenge: make <b>{0}</b>. Two digits, then the multiplier: how many zeros follow them.":`Tantangannya: buat <b>{0}</b>. Dua digit, lalu pengali: berapa nol yang mengikutinya.`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>1st digit</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>2nd digit</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 1k</b><small>multiplier</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>tolerance</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>digit ke-1</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>digit ke-2</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 1k</b><small>pengali</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>toleransi</small></span>`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>1st digit</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>2nd digit</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 10k</b><small>multiplier</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>tolerance</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>digit ke-1</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>digit ke-2</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 10k</b><small>pengali</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>toleransi</small></span>`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>1st digit</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>2nd digit</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 100k</b><small>multiplier</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>tolerance</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>digit ke-1</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>digit ke-2</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 100k</b><small>pengali</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>toleransi</small></span>`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>1st digit</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>2nd digit</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 1M</b><small>multiplier</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>tolerance</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>digit ke-1</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>digit ke-2</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>× 1M</b><small>pengali</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>±{2}</b><small>toleransi</small></span>`,"Resistors in series":`Resistor seri`,"{0}. Series<br />circuit":`{0}. Rangkaian<br />seri`,"One after another, resistors make the current push through each of them in turn. Their resistances simply add up — so the LED gets less current.":`Satu demi satu, resistor membuat arus harus melewati masing-masing secara bergiliran. Hambatannya tinggal dijumlahkan — jadi LED mendapat arus lebih kecil.`,"Total resistance = R1 + R2":`Hambatan total = R1 + R2`,"The same current flows through both":`Arus yang sama melewati keduanya`,"Click either resistor to change it":`Klik salah satu resistor untuk menggantinya`,"First in line.<br />Click to change it.":`Yang pertama di barisan.<br />Klik untuk menggantinya.`,"The same current<br />flows through it.":`Arus yang sama<br />melewatinya.`,"Dimmer: the total<br />resistance went up.":`Lebih redup: hambatan<br />totalnya naik.`,"In series the resistances add up:":`Dalam rangkaian seri, hambatan dijumlahkan:`,"R = {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>":`R = {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>`,"The LED still keeps {0}, leaving {1} for the pair:":`LED tetap mengambil {0}, menyisakan {1} untuk pasangan resistor:`,"Every bit of that current goes through both resistors. Each takes a share of the voltage in proportion to its size: R1 {0}, R2 {1}.":`Seluruh arus itu melewati kedua resistor. Masing-masing mengambil bagian tegangan sebanding dengan nilainya: R1 {0}, R2 {1}.`,"Resistor R1":`Resistor R1`,"Resistor R2":`Resistor R2`,"uses {0}":`memakai {0}`,"Resistors in parallel":`Resistor paralel`,"{0}. Parallel<br />circuit":`{0}. Rangkaian<br />paralel`,"Side by side, resistors give the current more than one path. The current splits between them, and the total resistance drops below even the smallest one.":`Bersebelahan, resistor memberi arus lebih dari satu jalur. Arus terbagi di antaranya, dan hambatan total turun bahkan di bawah yang terkecil.`,"Two paths: the current splits":`Dua jalur: arus terbagi`,"Most of it takes the easier path":`Sebagian besar memilih jalur yang lebih mudah`,"One path for<br />the current.":`Satu jalur untuk<br />arus.`,"A second path,<br />side by side.":`Jalur kedua,<br />bersebelahan.`,"Brighter: two paths<br />let more through.":`Lebih terang: dua jalur<br />melewatkan lebih banyak.`,"In parallel the paths share the work. Two resistors together make:":`Dalam rangkaian paralel, jalur-jalurnya berbagi kerja. Dua resistor bersama-sama menjadi:`,"R = {0} × {1} ÷ {2} = <b>{3}</b>":`R = {0} × {1} ÷ {2} = <b>{3}</b>`,"Both get the same {0}, so each passes its own current (Ohm’s law again):":`Keduanya mendapat {0} yang sama, jadi masing-masing melewatkan arusnya sendiri (hukum Ohm lagi):`,"They meet again before the LED: {0} + {1} = {2}.":`Keduanya bertemu lagi sebelum LED: {0} + {1} = {2}.`,"Voltage divider":`Pembagi tegangan`,"{0}. Voltage<br />divider":`{0}. Pembagi<br />tegangan`,"Two resistors in series share the supply’s voltage between them, in proportion to their resistance. A meter across each one shows its share — and the two shares always add up to the {0} the supply gives. The point in the middle sits at a voltage set by the ratio: a trick used all over electronics.":`Dua resistor seri berbagi tegangan catu daya di antara keduanya, sebanding dengan hambatannya. Alat ukur di setiap resistor menunjukkan bagiannya — dan kedua bagian itu selalu berjumlah {0} yang diberikan catu daya. Titik di tengah berada pada tegangan yang ditentukan oleh perbandingannya: trik yang dipakai di mana-mana dalam elektronika.`,"A meter across each resistor":`Alat ukur di setiap resistor`,"V1 + V2 = the supply’s {0}":`V1 + V2 = {0} dari catu daya`,"Change R1 or R2: the split follows the ratio":`Ganti R1 atau R2: pembagiannya mengikuti perbandingan`,"R1 (top)":`R1 (atas)`,"From + to the<br />middle point.":`Dari + ke<br />titik tengah.`,"R2 (bottom)":`R2 (bawah)`,"From the middle<br />point to −.":`Dari titik tengah<br />ke −.`,"Meter · V1":`Alat ukur · V1`,"Reads the voltage<br />across R1.":`Membaca tegangan<br />pada R1.`,"Meter · V2":`Alat ukur · V2`,"Reads the voltage<br />across R2.":`Membaca tegangan<br />pada R2.`,"The same current flows through both resistors:":`Arus yang sama melewati kedua resistor:`,"Each one’s share of the voltage is that current times its resistance (Ohm’s law), so the bigger resistor takes the bigger share:":`Bagian tegangan masing-masing adalah arus itu dikali hambatannya (hukum Ohm), jadi resistor yang lebih besar mengambil bagian yang lebih besar:`,"Together they make the whole supply: {0} + {1} = {2}. The middle point sits at V2, which in one line is":`Bersama-sama membentuk seluruh catu daya: {0} + {1} = {2}. Titik tengah berada pada V2, yang dalam satu baris adalah`,"Only the ratio matters: {0} and {1} split it the same way as {2} and {3}.":`Hanya perbandingannya yang penting: {0} dan {1} membaginya sama seperti {2} dan {3}.`,"That is true as long as nothing else draws current from the middle. Connect something there (a meter on V barely counts: about {0}) and it sits in parallel with R2, pulling the middle down. Keep whatever you connect at least ten times bigger than the divider’s resistors, or use smaller ones.":`Itu berlaku selama tidak ada hal lain yang mengambil arus dari titik tengah. Sambungkan sesuatu di sana (alat ukur mode volt hampir tidak berpengaruh: sekitar {0}) dan ia menjadi paralel dengan R2, menarik titik tengah turun. Pastikan apa pun yang kamu sambungkan setidaknya sepuluh kali lebih besar daripada resistor pembagi, atau pakai resistor yang lebih kecil.`,"Two multimeters":`Dua multimeter`,"set to V, one across each resistor":`pada mode V, satu di setiap resistor`,"Variable resistor":`Resistor variabel`,"{0}. Variable<br />resistor":`{0}. Resistor<br />variabel`,"A potentiometer is a resistor with a slider inside. Turn the knob and the resistance between its middle leg and an end changes smoothly — like turning a volume knob, or an old-fashioned dimmer.":`Potensiometer adalah resistor dengan penggeser di dalamnya. Putar kenopnya dan hambatan antara kaki tengah dan salah satu ujungnya berubah dengan mulus — seperti memutar kenop volume, atau peredup lampu model lama.`,"Drag around the knob to turn it":`Seret mengelilingi kenop untuk memutarnya`,"{0} to {1}, plus {2} to be safe":`{0} sampai {1}, ditambah {2} agar aman`,"The LED follows the knob":`LED mengikuti kenop`,Potentiometer:`Potensiometer`,"Drag around the<br />knob to turn it.":`Seret mengelilingi<br />kenop untuk memutarnya.`,"Keeps the LED safe<br />at full turn.":`Menjaga LED tetap aman<br />saat diputar penuh.`,"Dims and brightens<br />with the knob.":`Redup dan terang<br />mengikuti kenop.`,Knob:`Kenop`,"Between its middle leg (the wiper) and one end, the pot gives anything from {0} to {1}:":`Di antara kaki tengahnya (penggeser) dan satu ujung, potensiometer memberi nilai berapa pun dari {0} sampai {1}:`,"The fixed {0} is in series with it:":`{0} tetap dirangkai seri dengannya:`,"Why the {0}? Turned all the way up, the pot is {1} — without it nothing would hold the current back.":`Mengapa {0}? Diputar penuh, potensiometer bernilai {1} — tanpanya tidak ada yang menahan arus.`,"Pot {0}":`Pot. {0}`,"{0} · now {1}":`{0} · sekarang {1}`,"One way only":`Hanya satu arah`,"{0}. One way<br />only":`{0}. Hanya satu<br />arah`,"An LED is a diode: it lets current through in one direction only. The long leg (the anode) goes towards +, the short leg (the cathode, by the flat edge of the rim) towards −. Turn it round and it blocks the current, and stays dark.":`LED adalah dioda: melewatkan arus hanya ke satu arah. Kaki panjang (anoda) mengarah ke +, kaki pendek (katoda, di sisi pinggiran yang rata) ke −. Balikkan dan LED menghalangi arus, lalu tetap padam.`,"Long leg to +, short leg to −":`Kaki panjang ke +, kaki pendek ke −`,"Backwards, no current flows at all":`Terbalik, tidak ada arus sama sekali`,"Click the LED to turn it round":`Klik LED untuk membaliknya`,"Power Supply":`Catu daya`,"+ goes through the resistor<br />to the LED’s long leg.":`+ melewati resistor<br />ke kaki panjang LED.`,"Click it to turn it<br />the other way round.":`Klik untuk membaliknya<br />ke arah sebaliknya.`,"Keeps the current<br />in check.":`Menjaga arus<br />tetap terkendali.`,"Which way round":`Arah pemasangan`,"Long leg to +":`Kaki panjang ke +`,"Current flows from the long leg (anode) to the short one (cathode): it lights.":`Arus mengalir dari kaki panjang (anoda) ke kaki pendek (katoda): LED menyala.`,"Long leg to −":`Kaki panjang ke −`,"Backwards: the LED blocks the current and nothing flows.":`Terbalik: LED menghalangi arus dan tidak ada yang mengalir.`,"The right way round, the LED keeps about {0} and the resistor takes the rest:":`Dengan arah yang benar, LED mengambil sekitar {0} dan resistor mengambil sisanya:`,"Turn it round and see what happens to the numbers.":`Balikkan dan lihat apa yang terjadi pada angkanya.`,"long leg to +":`kaki panjang ke +`,"thick, on the bench":`tebal, di atas meja`,blocked:`terhalang`,"Backwards, the LED blocks:":`Terbalik, LED menghalangi:`,"With no current, the resistor has nothing to drop (V = I × R = {0}), so the whole {1} sits across the LED — but it still won’t let any through.":`Tanpa arus, resistor tidak menurunkan apa pun (V = I × R = {0}), jadi seluruh {1} berada pada LED — tapi LED tetap tidak melewatkan apa pun.`,"An LED only takes about {0} backwards before it breaks down, so don’t push your luck with bigger voltages.":`LED hanya tahan sekitar {0} secara terbalik sebelum rusak, jadi jangan ambil risiko dengan tegangan yang lebih besar.`,backwards:`terbalik`,"long leg to −":`kaki panjang ke −`,"Colours and volts":`Warna dan volt`,"{0}. Colours<br />& volts":`{0}. Warna<br />& volt`,"Every colour needs its own voltage":`Setiap warna butuh tegangannya sendiri`,"Each colour of LED needs a different voltage before it lights: red about {0}, green a little more, blue and white about {1}. {2} only just reaches a blue LED; {3} is plenty.":`Setiap warna LED butuh tegangan berbeda sebelum menyala: merah sekitar {0}, hijau sedikit lebih tinggi, biru dan putih sekitar {1}. {2} baru cukup untuk LED biru; {3} lebih dari cukup.`,"Click the LED to change its colour":`Klik LED untuk mengganti warnanya`,"Click the supply for {0} or {1}":`Klik catu daya untuk {0} atau {1}`,"Blue and white need about {0}":`Biru dan putih butuh sekitar {0}`,"Pick {0} or {1}<br />in its settings.":`Pilih {0} atau {1}<br />di pengaturannya.`,"Click it to try<br />another colour.":`Klik untuk mencoba<br />warna lain.`,"Takes the voltage<br />the LED leaves.":`Mengambil tegangan<br />yang ditinggalkan LED.`,"Plenty for red, yellow and green.":`Cukup untuk merah, kuning, dan hijau.`,"Enough for any colour.":`Cukup untuk warna apa pun.`,"The LED keeps its forward voltage; the resistor gets whatever is left:":`LED mempertahankan tegangan majunya; resistor mendapat sisanya:`,"<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>red</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>yellow</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>{2}</b><small>green</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>{3}</b><small>blue</small></span><span>{t4}</span><b>{4}</b><small>white</small></span>":`<span>{t0}</span><b>{0}</b><small>merah</small></span><span>{t1}</span><b>{1}</b><small>kuning</small></span><span>{t2}</span><b>{2}</b><small>hijau</small></span><span>{t3}</span><b>{3}</b><small>biru</small></span><span>{t4}</span><b>{4}</b><small>putih</small></span>`,"Bluer light carries more energy, so blue LEDs need more voltage. A white LED is a blue one inside, coated with a yellow phosphor that turns some of its blue light into the rest of the colours — so it needs a blue LED’s voltage too.":`Cahaya yang lebih biru membawa lebih banyak energi, jadi LED biru butuh tegangan lebih tinggi. LED putih sebenarnya LED biru di dalamnya, dilapisi fosfor kuning yang mengubah sebagian cahaya birunya menjadi warna-warna lain — jadi ia juga butuh tegangan LED biru.`,"Green comes in two kinds: the classic yellowish green here needs about {0}, but a bright “true green” LED is made like a blue one and needs about {1}.":`Hijau ada dua jenis: hijau kekuningan klasik di sini butuh sekitar {0}, tetapi LED “hijau murni” yang terang dibuat seperti LED biru dan butuh sekitar {1}.`,"needs {0}":`butuh {0}`,"Yellow LED":`LED kuning`,"{0} − {1} = only {2}":`{0} − {1} = hanya {2}`,"Almost nothing is left over, so the formula says no current at all. In fact an LED’s voltage isn’t a sharp edge: just below it a little current still creeps through — here <b>{0}</b>, enough for only the faintest glow. It needs more volts.":`Hampir tidak ada yang tersisa, jadi rumusnya mengatakan tidak ada arus sama sekali. Sebenarnya tegangan LED bukan batas yang tajam: sedikit di bawahnya masih ada sedikit arus yang merembes — di sini <b>{0}</b>, hanya cukup untuk pendar yang sangat samar. LED butuh volt lebih banyak.`,"Blue LED":`LED biru`,"{0} − {1} = less than nothing":`{0} − {1} = kurang dari nol`,"The supply doesn’t even reach the LED’s voltage, so the formula says no current at all. In fact an LED’s voltage isn’t a sharp edge: just below it a little current still creeps through — here <b>{0}</b>, enough for only the faintest glow. It needs more volts.":`Catu daya bahkan tidak mencapai tegangan LED, jadi rumusnya mengatakan tidak ada arus sama sekali. Sebenarnya tegangan LED bukan batas yang tajam: sedikit di bawahnya masih ada sedikit arus yang merembes — di sini <b>{0}</b>, hanya cukup untuk pendar yang sangat samar. LED butuh volt lebih banyak.`,"White LED":`LED putih`,"Too much current":`Arus terlalu besar`,"{0}. Too much<br />current":`{0}. Arus terlalu<br />besar`,"An LED doesn’t know when to stop: past its forward voltage, the current shoots up. The resistor is what holds it back. Take the resistor away and the LED gets several times its {0}, for about a second.":`LED tidak tahu kapan harus berhenti: melewati tegangan majunya, arus melonjak. Resistorlah yang menahannya. Lepas resistornya dan LED mendapat beberapa kali {0}-nya, selama sekitar satu detik.`,"Smaller resistor, more current":`Resistor lebih kecil, arus lebih besar`,"About {0} is plenty for an LED":`Sekitar {0} sudah cukup untuk LED`,"Without a resistor, it burns out":`Tanpa resistor, LED terbakar`,"Click it: try smaller<br />values, then none.":`Klik: coba nilai yang lebih<br />kecil, lalu tanpa resistor.`,"Happy with up to<br />about {0}.":`Senang dengan sampai<br />sekitar {0}.`,"In place of the resistor":`Pengganti resistor`,"About {0}: comfortable.":`Sekitar {0}: nyaman.`,"About {0}: bright.":`Sekitar {0}: terang.`,"About {0}: right at the limit.":`Sekitar {0}: tepat di batas.`,"Wire link":`Kabel penghubung`,"No resistor at all: around {0}. Goodbye, LED.":`Tanpa resistor sama sekali: sekitar {0}. Selamat tinggal, LED.`,"The LED keeps {0}, the resistor holds the current back:":`LED mengambil {0}, resistor menahan arus:`,"Well inside the LED’s {0}.":`Jauh di dalam batas {0} LED.`,"up to {0}":`sampai {0}`,"That is right at the LED’s limit: it will be bright, and warm.":`Itu tepat di batas LED: akan terang, dan hangat.`,"With a plain wire there is nothing left to hold the current back but the LED’s own few ohms and the supply’s:":`Dengan kabel biasa, tidak ada lagi yang menahan arus selain beberapa ohm dari LED itu sendiri dan dari catu daya:`,"Five times what it can take. The heat in its tiny chip:":`Lima kali dari yang bisa ditahannya. Panas di cipnya yang mungil:`,"Every LED needs something to limit its current, usually a resistor.":`Setiap LED butuh sesuatu untuk membatasi arusnya, biasanya resistor.`,"wire link":`kabel penghubung`,"no resistance":`tanpa hambatan`,"The plain diode":`Dioda biasa`,"{0}. The plain<br />diode":`{0}. Dioda<br />biasa`,"A plain diode is an LED without the light: a one-way valve for current. The black band marks the cathode, and current flows towards it. Getting through costs about {0} — on a {1} supply that is a big part of what the LED’s resistor had, so the LED gets much less current.":`Dioda biasa adalah LED tanpa cahaya: katup satu arah untuk arus. Gelang hitam menandai katoda, dan arus mengalir ke arahnya. Melewatinya memakan sekitar {0} — pada catu daya {1} itu bagian besar dari yang dimiliki resistor LED, jadi LED mendapat arus jauh lebih kecil.`,"Current flows towards the band":`Arus mengalir ke arah gelang`,"Turn it round and it blocks":`Balikkan dan ia menghalangi`,"It keeps about {0} for itself":`Ia mengambil sekitar {0} untuk dirinya`,Diode:`Dioda`,"The band is the cathode.<br />Click to turn it round.":`Gelang adalah katoda.<br />Klik untuk membaliknya.`,"Dimmer: the diode<br />took {0}.":`Lebih redup: dioda<br />mengambil {0}.`,"Gets what the diode<br />and LED leave.":`Mendapat sisa dari dioda<br />dan LED.`,"Band to the LED":`Gelang ke arah LED`,"Current flows towards the band: it goes through.":`Arus mengalir ke arah gelang: arus lewat.`,"Band to +":`Gelang ke arah +`,"Backwards: the diode blocks.":`Terbalik: dioda menghalangi.`,"The diode keeps {0}, the LED {1}, and the resistor gets the rest:":`Dioda mengambil {0}, LED {1}, dan resistor mendapat sisanya:`,"Without the diode it would be {0}: those {1} cost the LED most of its current.":`Tanpa dioda nilainya {0}: {1} itu membuat LED kehilangan sebagian besar arusnya.`,"1N4148 diode":`Dioda 1N4148`,"band towards the LED":`gelang ke arah LED`,"Backwards, the diode blocks:":`Terbalik, dioda menghalangi:`,"With no current, neither the resistor nor the LED drops anything, so the whole {0} sits across the diode.":`Tanpa arus, baik resistor maupun LED tidak menurunkan apa pun, jadi seluruh {0} berada pada dioda.`,"That’s why diodes guard circuits against batteries put in the wrong way round.":`Itulah sebabnya dioda melindungi rangkaian dari baterai yang terpasang terbalik.`,"band towards +":`gelang ke arah +`,"LEDs in series":`LED seri`,"{0}. LEDs in<br />series":`{0}. LED<br />seri`,"Two LEDs in a row share one current, but each needs its own voltage: about {0} for a red one. Together that is {1}, more than {2} can give. Turn the supply up to {3} and both light up.":`Dua LED berderet berbagi satu arus, tapi masing-masing butuh tegangannya sendiri: sekitar {0} untuk LED merah. Bersama-sama {1}, lebih dari yang bisa diberikan {2}. Naikkan catu daya ke {3} dan keduanya menyala.`,"Each red LED needs about {0}":`Setiap LED merah butuh sekitar {0}`,"In series their voltages add up":`Dalam seri tegangannya dijumlahkan`,"Click the supply for {0}":`Klik catu daya untuk {0}`,"{0} for now.<br />Turn it up to {1}.":`{0} untuk sekarang.<br />Naikkan ke {1}.`,"LED {0}":`LED {0}`,"Needs about {0}.":`Butuh sekitar {0}.`,"Needs another {0}.<br />Click to change colour.":`Butuh {0} lagi.<br />Klik untuk mengganti warna.`,"Not enough for two LEDs.":`Tidak cukup untuk dua LED.`,"Enough for both, with a little to spare.":`Cukup untuk keduanya, dengan sedikit sisa.`,"In series the LEDs’ voltages add up:":`Dalam seri tegangan LED dijumlahkan:`,"The supply’s {0} is less than the {1} the pair needs, so nothing is left to push current through the {2}. An LED’s voltage isn’t a sharp edge, but {3} short is far too much: practically no current flows, and both stay dark.":`{0} dari catu daya lebih kecil daripada {1} yang dibutuhkan pasangan LED, jadi tidak ada yang tersisa untuk mendorong arus melewati resistor {2}. Tegangan LED bukan batas yang tajam, tapi kurang {3} itu terlalu banyak: praktis tidak ada arus yang mengalir, dan keduanya tetap padam.`,"That is why torches and fairy lights with several LEDs in a row run on higher voltages — or put the LEDs side by side instead, each with its own resistor.":`Itulah sebabnya senter dan lampu hias dengan beberapa LED berderet memakai tegangan lebih tinggi — atau memasang LED bersebelahan, masing-masing dengan resistornya sendiri.`,"Whatever the supply has beyond that pushes current through the {0}:":`Kelebihan tegangan catu daya di atas itu mendorong arus melewati resistor {0}:`,"The same current lights both LEDs.":`Arus yang sama menyalakan kedua LED.`,"Like a water tank":`Seperti tangki air`,"{0}. Like a<br />water tank":`{0}. Seperti<br />tangki air`,"A capacitor is like a water tank":`Kapasitor itu seperti tangki air`,"Before the electronics, a picture with water. A supply tank on legs is kept full, like a battery holding its voltage. Open the tap and water flows down through a narrow pipe into a glass tank. It fills quickly at first, then slower and slower, and stops when its water is as high as the supply’s — exactly how a capacitor fills through a resistor.":`Sebelum elektronika, gambaran dengan air. Tangki pasokan di atas kaki-kaki dijaga tetap penuh, seperti baterai yang mempertahankan tegangannya. Buka keran dan air mengalir turun lewat pipa sempit ke tangki kaca. Tangki terisi cepat pada awalnya, lalu makin lama makin lambat, dan berhenti saat airnya setinggi air tangki pasokan — persis seperti kapasitor terisi melalui resistor.`,"Open the tap and watch it fill":`Buka keran dan lihat tangki terisi`,"A wider tank holds more: more capacitance":`Tangki lebih lebar menampung lebih banyak: kapasitansi lebih besar`,"A narrower pipe fills it slower: more resistance":`Pipa lebih sempit mengisinya lebih lambat: hambatan lebih besar`,"Supply Tank":`Tangki pasokan`,"Kept full, like<br />a battery.":`Selalu penuh, seperti<br />baterai.`,Tap:`Keran`,"Click it to open<br />or shut it.":`Klik untuk membuka<br />atau menutupnya.`,"Narrow Pipe":`Pipa sempit`,"Holds the flow<br />back: a resistor.":`Menahan aliran:<br />sebuah resistor.`,"Glass Tank":`Tangki kaca`,"Fills like<br />a capacitor.":`Terisi seperti<br />kapasitor.`,Drain:`Saluran buang`,"Hold it to<br />empty the tank.":`Tahan untuk<br />mengosongkan tangki.`,Tank:`Tangki`,Small:`Kecil`,"Fills to the top quickly: little capacitance.":`Cepat penuh sampai atas: kapasitansi kecil.`,Medium:`Sedang`,"About twice the water for the same height.":`Sekitar dua kali air untuk ketinggian yang sama.`,Large:`Besar`,"Holds the most, so takes longest to fill: lots of capacitance.":`Menampung paling banyak, jadi paling lama terisi: kapasitansi besar.`,Pipe:`Pipa`,Narrow:`Sempit`,"Holds the flow back hard: like a big resistor.":`Menahan aliran dengan kuat: seperti resistor besar.`,"In between.":`Di antaranya.`,Wide:`Lebar`,"Lets the water rush in: like a small resistor.":`Membiarkan air mengalir deras: seperti resistor kecil.`,"Water in the tank":`Air di tangki`,"{0} · after one τ":`{0} · setelah satu τ`,"Every part has an electrical twin:":`Setiap bagian punya kembaran listriknya:`,Water:`Air`,Electricity:`Listrik`,"the supply’s height of water":`ketinggian air tangki pasokan`,"the battery’s voltage":`tegangan baterai`,"the height of water in the tank":`ketinggian air di tangki`,"the capacitor’s voltage":`tegangan kapasitor`,"how much water is in the tank":`banyaknya air di tangki`,"the charge it holds":`muatan yang disimpannya`,"the flow along the pipe":`aliran di dalam pipa`,"the current":`arus`,"the narrow pipe":`pipa sempit`,"the resistor":`resistor`,"a wider tank":`tangki yang lebih lebar`,"more capacitance":`kapasitansi lebih besar`,"the tap":`keran`,"the switch":`sakelar`,"the drain":`saluran buang`,"the push button that empties it":`tombol tekan yang mengosongkannya`,"The water is pushed along by the <i>difference</i> between the two heights: {0} in the supply, {1} in the tank now. As the tank fills, the difference shrinks, so the flow slows — which is why the level creeps up more and more slowly and never quite reaches the supply’s. A capacitor’s current falls off the same way as its voltage catches up with the battery’s.":`Air didorong oleh <i>selisih</i> kedua ketinggian: {0} di tangki pasokan, {1} di tangki sekarang. Saat tangki terisi, selisihnya mengecil, jadi alirannya melambat — itulah sebabnya permukaan air naik makin lama makin lambat dan tidak pernah benar-benar mencapai ketinggian tangki pasokan. Arus kapasitor juga berkurang dengan cara yang sama saat tegangannya mendekati tegangan baterai.`,"How long it takes depends on both the pipe and the tank: a narrower pipe lets less through, a wider tank needs more water for each centimetre. In a circuit that is the time constant,":`Lamanya bergantung pada pipa dan tangki: pipa yang lebih sempit melewatkan lebih sedikit, tangki yang lebih lebar butuh lebih banyak air untuk setiap sentimeter. Dalam rangkaian, itulah konstanta waktu,`,"Here that works out at about <b>{0}</b>: after one τ the tank is {1} full ({2}), after five as good as full.":`Di sini hasilnya sekitar <b>{0}</b>: setelah satu τ tangki terisi {1} ({2}), setelah lima τ hampir penuh.`,"Water is only a picture: a capacitor doesn’t hold any extra electrons overall. Charge piles up on one plate and leaves the other, which is why there are two wires — but the way it fills and empties is just the same.":`Air hanyalah gambaran: secara keseluruhan kapasitor tidak menyimpan elektron tambahan. Muatan menumpuk di satu keping dan meninggalkan keping lain, itulah sebabnya ada dua kabel — tapi cara terisi dan kosongnya sama persis.`,"tap shut":`keran tertutup`,"medium pipe":`pipa sedang`,"medium tank":`tangki sedang`,drain:`saluran buang`,"Supply tank":`Tangki pasokan`,"kept full: {0} of water, the “{1}”":`selalu penuh: {0} air, “{1}”`,"Medium pipe":`Pipa sedang`,"Medium glass tank":`Tangki kaca sedang`,"the capacitor":`kapasitor`,"tap open":`keran terbuka`,"small tank":`tangki kecil`,"Small glass tank":`Tangki kaca kecil`,"large tank":`tangki besar`,"Large glass tank":`Tangki kaca besar`,"narrow pipe":`pipa sempit`,"Narrow pipe":`Pipa sempit`,"wide pipe":`pipa lebar`,"Wide pipe":`Pipa lebar`,"Charge it up":`Isi muatan`,"{0}. Charge<br />it up":`{0}. Isi<br />muatan`,"A capacitor stores charge":`Kapasitor menyimpan muatan`,"A capacitor is two metal plates with a thin insulator between them. Connect it to a power supply and charge piles up on the plates until its voltage matches the supply’s. Then it holds that charge, even with the power switched off.":`Kapasitor adalah dua keping logam dengan isolator tipis di antaranya. Hubungkan ke catu daya dan muatan menumpuk di keping-kepingnya sampai tegangannya sama dengan tegangan catu daya. Lalu ia menahan muatan itu, bahkan saat daya dimatikan.`,"It fills until it matches the supply":`Terisi sampai sama dengan catu daya`,"The resistor sets how fast it fills":`Resistor menentukan seberapa cepat terisi`,"Hold the button down to empty it":`Tahan tombol untuk mengosongkannya`,"Switch it on to fill<br />the capacitor up.":`Nyalakan untuk mengisi<br />kapasitor.`,Capacitor:`Kapasitor`,"Its voltage climbs<br />as it fills.":`Tegangannya naik<br />saat terisi.`,"Push Button":`Tombol tekan`,"Hold it down to<br />empty the capacitor.":`Tahan untuk<br />mengosongkan kapasitor.`,"Bigger, and it<br />fills more slowly.":`Lebih besar, dan<br />terisi lebih lambat.`,"Fills in about {0} with {1}.":`Terisi dalam sekitar {0} dengan {1}.`,Capacitance:`Kapasitansi`,"Holds {0} µC at {1}.":`Menyimpan {0} µC pada {1}.`,"Capacitor voltage":`Tegangan kapasitor`,"How quickly it fills depends on the resistor and the capacitor together, the <i>time constant</i>:":`Seberapa cepat terisi bergantung pada resistor dan kapasitor bersama-sama, yaitu <i>konstanta waktu</i>:`,"After one τ it is {0} full ({1}); after five it is as good as full. The current is biggest at the start and shrinks as it fills:":`Setelah satu τ terisi {0} ({1}); setelah lima τ hampir penuh. Arusnya paling besar di awal dan mengecil saat terisi:`,"The charge it holds now:":`Muatan yang disimpannya sekarang:`,"A real electrolytic isn’t a perfect insulator inside: left charged, it slowly leaks its charge away, over minutes to hours. Big capacitors can hold a charge for a while, which is why the insides of mains equipment can still be dangerous after it is unplugged.":`Kapasitor elektrolit sungguhan bukan isolator sempurna di dalamnya: jika dibiarkan bermuatan, muatannya perlahan bocor, dalam hitungan menit sampai jam. Kapasitor besar bisa menahan muatan cukup lama, itulah sebabnya bagian dalam peralatan listrik rumah bisa tetap berbahaya setelah dicabut.`,button:`tombol`,"{0} electrolytic":`Elektrolit {0}`,"Push button":`Tombol tekan`,"empties the capacitor":`mengosongkan kapasitor`,"Fading light":`Cahaya yang meredup`,"{0}. Fading<br />light":`{0}. Cahaya yang<br />meredup`,"A capacitor as a tiny battery":`Kapasitor seperti baterai mungil`,"With the power on, the capacitor fills up right beside the LED. Switch the power off and the capacitor takes over, pushing its charge through the LED, which fades as the capacitor empties.":`Saat daya menyala, kapasitor terisi tepat di samping LED. Matikan daya dan kapasitor mengambil alih, mendorong muatannya melewati LED, yang meredup saat kapasitor kosong.`,"It keeps the LED going for a moment":`Menjaga LED tetap menyala sebentar`,"The LED fades as it empties":`LED meredup saat kapasitor kosong`,"Bigger capacitor, longer glow":`Kapasitor lebih besar, cahaya lebih lama`,"Switch it off and<br />watch the LED.":`Matikan dan<br />perhatikan LED.`,"Click it to try a<br />bigger or smaller one.":`Klik untuk mencoba yang<br />lebih besar atau lebih kecil.`,"Runs on the capacitor<br />once the power’s off.":`Bekerja dengan kapasitor<br />setelah daya mati.`,"Gone in a fifth of a second.":`Hilang dalam seperlima detik.`,"Fades out over about a second.":`Meredup dalam sekitar satu detik.`,"A slow fade, about five seconds.":`Meredup perlahan, sekitar lima detik.`,"Full, the capacitor holds:":`Saat penuh, kapasitor menyimpan:`,"With the power off, the LED and its {0} drain that charge. The LED goes out once the capacitor drops to about {1}, so only the top volt or so is used. How fast depends on":`Saat daya mati, LED dan resistor {0}-nya menguras muatan itu. LED padam begitu kapasitor turun ke sekitar {1}, jadi hanya sekitar satu volt teratas yang terpakai. Kecepatannya bergantung pada`,"Ten times the capacitance, ten times the glow.":`Sepuluh kali kapasitansi, sepuluh kali cahaya.`,on:`menyala`,"Only while charging":`Hanya saat mengisi`,"{0}. Only while<br />charging":`{0}. Hanya saat<br />mengisi`,"Current only while it charges":`Arus hanya saat mengisi`,"Put a capacitor in line with an LED and current flows only while the capacitor is filling: the LED flashes and goes out. Once it is charged, no more current gets through — until you empty it again.":`Pasang kapasitor secara seri dengan LED dan arus hanya mengalir saat kapasitor terisi: LED berkedip lalu padam. Setelah terisi, tidak ada arus lagi yang lewat — sampai kamu mengosongkannya lagi.`,"A charged capacitor blocks steady current":`Kapasitor yang terisi menghalangi arus tetap`,"The LED flashes while it fills":`LED berkedip saat kapasitor terisi`,"Hold the button to empty it":`Tahan tombol untuk mengosongkannya`,"Flashes while the<br />capacitor fills.":`Berkedip saat<br />kapasitor terisi.`,"In line with the LED:<br />full, it blocks.":`Seri dengan LED:<br />saat penuh, menghalangi.`,"A quick flash, under half a second.":`Kedipan cepat, kurang dari setengah detik.`,"A longer flash, a second or two.":`Kedipan lebih lama, satu atau dua detik.`,"The capacitor fills until it holds the supply’s voltage, less what the LED needs:":`Kapasitor terisi sampai mendapat tegangan catu daya, dikurangi yang dibutuhkan LED:`,"After that nothing is left to push current through the LED, so it stays dark. While it fills, the current is":`Setelah itu tidak ada lagi yang mendorong arus melewati LED, jadi LED tetap padam. Saat terisi, arusnya adalah`,"This is why capacitors block steady (DC) current but pass changes — the basis of filters and timers.":`Itulah sebabnya kapasitor menghalangi arus tetap (DC) tapi melewatkan perubahan — dasar dari filter dan pewaktu.`,"It is there: the capacitor has {0}, so the LED and resistor have nothing left to push current with, and the LED is dark. (The capacitor creeps a little past {1}: an LED’s voltage isn’t a sharp edge, and a trickle — {2} now — still gets through, far too little to see.)":`Sudah: kapasitor bertegangan {0}, jadi LED dan resistor tidak punya apa-apa lagi untuk mendorong arus, dan LED padam. (Kapasitor sedikit melewati {1}: tegangan LED bukan batas yang tajam, dan arus kecil — {2} sekarang — masih lewat, terlalu kecil untuk terlihat.)`,"In series & parallel":`Seri & paralel`,"{0}. Series &<br />parallel":`{0}. Seri &<br />paralel`,"Two capacitors: series and parallel":`Dua kapasitor: seri dan paralel`,"Side by side — in parallel — two capacitors act like one bigger one: their capacitances add, so together they hold more and take longer to fill. One after the other — in series — they act like a smaller one: two the same make half the capacitance, and fill twice as fast. It is the opposite of resistors.":`Bersebelahan — paralel — dua kapasitor bertindak seperti satu kapasitor yang lebih besar: kapasitansinya dijumlahkan, jadi bersama-sama menyimpan lebih banyak dan lebih lama terisi. Satu setelah yang lain — seri — keduanya bertindak seperti kapasitor yang lebih kecil: dua yang sama menghasilkan setengah kapasitansi, dan terisi dua kali lebih cepat. Kebalikan dari resistor.`,"Parallel: the capacitances add":`Paralel: kapasitansinya dijumlahkan`,"Series: smaller than either one":`Seri: lebih kecil dari masing-masing`,"The chart shows how fast they fill":`Grafik menunjukkan seberapa cepat keduanya terisi`,"Switch it on to fill<br />the capacitors up.":`Nyalakan untuk mengisi<br />kapasitor-kapasitornya.`,"Click one to wire them<br />in series or parallel.":`Klik salah satu untuk merangkainya<br />seri atau paralel.`,"Hold it down to<br />empty them.":`Tahan untuk<br />mengosongkannya.`,One:`Satu`,"{0} on its own: τ = {1} × {2} ≈ {3}.":`{0} saja: τ = {1} × {2} ≈ {3}.`,"Together {0}: they fill twice as fast.":`Bersama {0}: terisi dua kali lebih cepat.`,"Together {0}: they take twice as long.":`Bersama {0}: dua kali lebih lama.`,"Voltage across the capacitors":`Tegangan pada kapasitor`,"In parallel the capacitances simply add, like making the plates bigger:":`Dalam paralel kapasitansi tinggal dijumlahkan, seperti memperbesar keping-kepingnya:`,"C = {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>":`C = {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>`,"Both have the same voltage across them; the charging current splits between them, {0} each now.":`Keduanya punya tegangan yang sama; arus pengisian terbagi di antaranya, masing-masing {0} sekarang.`,"With the {0} resistor, the time constant is":`Dengan resistor {0}, konstanta waktunya adalah`,"so they are as good as full after about five τ: {0}.":`jadi keduanya hampir penuh setelah sekitar lima τ: {0}.`,"Resistors do it the other way round: in series they add, in parallel they make less. That is because a capacitor’s value comes from the area of its plates (parallel: more area) and the gap between them (series: a wider gap).":`Resistor melakukannya sebaliknya: dalam seri dijumlahkan, dalam paralel menjadi lebih kecil. Itu karena nilai kapasitor berasal dari luas kepingnya (paralel: luas lebih besar) dan jarak di antaranya (seri: jarak lebih lebar).`,"{0} × {1} electrolytic":`{0} × elektrolit {1}`,"empties them":`mengosongkannya`,"One {0} capacitor on its own:":`Satu kapasitor {0} saja:`,"so it is as good as full after about five τ: {0}.":`jadi kapasitor hampir penuh setelah sekitar lima τ: {0}.`,"In series the capacitances combine like resistors in parallel:":`Dalam seri, kapasitansi bergabung seperti resistor paralel:`,"{0} ÷ C = {1} ÷ {2} + {3} ÷ {4}, so C = <b>{5}</b>":`{0} ÷ C = {1} ÷ {2} + {3} ÷ {4}, jadi C = <b>{5}</b>`,"The same charge flows onto both, so two the same share the voltage: each has <b>{0}</b> now, half of the total.":`Muatan yang sama mengalir ke keduanya, jadi dua kapasitor yang sama berbagi tegangan: masing-masing <b>{0}</b> sekarang, setengah dari total.`,Smoothing:`Perataan`,"{0}. Smoothing<br />AC to DC":`{0}. Meratakan<br />AC ke DC`,"Smoothing: from AC to steady DC":`Perataan: dari AC ke DC yang stabil`,"A diode lets an AC supply through one way only: what comes out is DC, but in bumps — on for half of each cycle, off for the other half. A capacitor across the output fills up at the top of each bump and keeps the current going in between. A bigger one sags less between bumps: the ripple gets smaller, and the LED shines steadily.":`Dioda melewatkan sumber AC hanya ke satu arah: yang keluar adalah DC, tapi berupa gundukan — ada selama separuh setiap siklus, tidak ada selama separuh lainnya. Kapasitor di keluaran terisi di puncak setiap gundukan dan menjaga arus tetap mengalir di antaranya. Kapasitor yang lebih besar turun lebih sedikit di antara gundukan: riaknya mengecil, dan LED menyala stabil.`,"The chart: bumps, and how much the capacitor fills in":`Grafik: gundukan, dan seberapa banyak kapasitor mengisinya`,"Click the capacitor to change its size":`Klik kapasitor untuk mengganti ukurannya`,"The diode lets only one way through":`Dioda hanya melewatkan satu arah`,"AC Adapter":`Adaptor AC`,"{0} peaks, {1} times<br />a second. Click to switch on.":`Puncak {0}, {1} kali<br />per detik. Klik untuk menyalakan.`,"Lets the current<br />through one way.":`Melewatkan arus<br />ke satu arah.`,"Fills at each peak,<br />feeds the LED between.":`Terisi di setiap puncak,<br />memberi daya LED di antaranya.`,"Smoothing capacitor":`Kapasitor perata`,None:`Tidak ada`,"Only the bumps: the LED is dark for more than half of each cycle.":`Hanya gundukan: LED padam lebih dari separuh setiap siklus.`,"It sags well over a volt between bumps.":`Turun jauh lebih dari satu volt di antara gundukan.`,"A ripple of about a third of a volt.":`Riak sekitar sepertiga volt.`,"Hardly any ripple: nearly steady DC.":`Hampir tidak ada riak: DC yang hampir stabil.`,Speed:`Kecepatan`,"{0} × slower":`{0} × lebih lambat`,"Two cycles a second, slow enough to watch the LED.":`Dua siklus per detik, cukup lambat untuk mengamati LED.`,"Real speed":`Kecepatan sebenarnya`,"{0} cycles a second: too fast for your eye, which sees the average.":`{0} siklus per detik: terlalu cepat untuk mata, yang melihat rata-ratanya.`,"Output · {0} × slower":`Keluaran · {0} × lebih lambat`,"the LED needs {0}":`LED butuh {0}`,"The adapter swings to {0} and back, {1} times a second. The diode only conducts while the wave is more than {2} above what is after it, so at best the output reaches":`Adaptor berayun sampai {0} dan kembali, {1} kali per detik. Dioda hanya menghantarkan saat gelombang lebih dari {2} di atas yang ada setelahnya, jadi paling tinggi keluarannya mencapai`,"and the LED and {0} take about {1} at that.":`dan LED serta resistor {0} mengambil sekitar {1} pada tegangan itu.`,"Between peaks (one every {0}) only the capacitor feeds them, and it sags by about":`Di antara puncak (satu setiap {0}) hanya kapasitor yang memberi daya, dan kapasitor turun sekitar`,"The chart measures <b>{0}</b> from top to bottom. Ten times the capacitance, a tenth of the ripple.":`Grafik mengukur <b>{0}</b> dari atas ke bawah. Sepuluh kali kapasitansi, sepersepuluh riak.`,"Mains power supplies work the same way, usually with four diodes (a bridge) so both halves of the wave are used and the bumps come twice as often — halving the ripple for the same capacitor. A regulator after the capacitor then irons out what is left. (Most chargers now are switch-mode supplies, which chop the current thousands of times a second to save weight — but there is still a rectifier and a smoothing capacitor inside.)":`Catu daya listrik rumah bekerja dengan cara yang sama, biasanya dengan empat dioda (sebuah jembatan) agar kedua separuh gelombang terpakai dan gundukannya datang dua kali lebih sering — membagi dua riak dengan kapasitor yang sama. Regulator setelah kapasitor lalu meratakan sisanya. (Kebanyakan pengisi daya sekarang adalah catu daya switching, yang mencacah arus ribuan kali per detik agar lebih ringan — tapi di dalamnya tetap ada penyearah dan kapasitor perata.)`,"AC adapter":`Adaptor AC`,"{0} peak, {1}":`Puncak {0}, {1}`,"1N4001 diode":`Dioda 1N4001`,"lets the current one way":`melewatkan arus ke satu arah`,"ripple {0}":`riak {0}`,"With no capacitor the output is just the bumps: zero for the whole negative half, and below the LED’s {0} for a good part of the rest. The LED is lit for only about a third of each cycle — at real speed your eye sees a dimmer, steady glow.":`Tanpa kapasitor, keluarannya hanya gundukan: nol selama seluruh separuh negatif, dan di bawah {0} yang dibutuhkan LED selama sebagian besar sisanya. LED menyala hanya sekitar sepertiga setiap siklus — pada kecepatan sebenarnya mata melihat pendar yang lebih redup dan stabil.`,"bumps only":`hanya gundukan`,"Output voltage":`Tegangan keluaran`,"Timed delay":`Tunda waktu`,"{0}. Timed<br />delay":`{0}. Tunda<br />waktu`,"A light that switches itself off":`Lampu yang mati sendiri`,"Like a stair light on a timer: press the button and the capacitor fills in an instant. Let go and the capacitor keeps a transistor switched on as it slowly empties through a {0} resistor — so the LED stays lit for a while, then fades out. A bigger capacitor lasts longer.":`Seperti lampu tangga dengan pewaktu: tekan tombol dan kapasitor terisi seketika. Lepaskan dan kapasitor menjaga transistor tetap aktif sambil perlahan kosong melalui resistor {0} — jadi LED tetap menyala sebentar, lalu meredup. Kapasitor yang lebih besar bertahan lebih lama.`,"Press the button, then let go":`Tekan tombol, lalu lepaskan`,"The capacitor empties into the base":`Kapasitor kosong ke basis`,"The chart shows it running down":`Grafik menunjukkan penurunannya`,"Press it, then let go:<br />the LED stays on.":`Tekan, lalu lepaskan:<br />LED tetap menyala.`,"Empties into the base,<br />keeping it switched on.":`Kosong ke basis,<br />menjaganya tetap aktif.`,"Stays fully on for about {0} after you let go, out after {1}.":`Tetap menyala penuh sekitar {0} setelah dilepas, padam setelah {1}.`,"below this, the LED fades":`di bawah ini, LED meredup`,"Pressed, the button joins the capacitor straight to the {0} supply: it is full in a few thousandths of a second. Let go, and the only way out for its charge is through the {1} to the transistor’s base, so it empties on a time scale of about":`Saat ditekan, tombol menghubungkan kapasitor langsung ke catu daya {0}: penuh dalam beberapa milidetik. Saat dilepas, satu-satunya jalan keluar bagi muatannya adalah melalui resistor {1} ke basis transistor, jadi kapasitor kosong dalam skala waktu sekitar`,"The LED needs {0}; with a gain of {1}, the base needs {2} to keep it fully on. The base sits at about {3}, where the {4} to the emitter takes another {5} — so the {6} has to carry both, and does while the capacitor stays above about <b>{7}</b>.":`LED butuh {0}; dengan penguatan {1}, basis butuh {2} agar LED tetap menyala penuh. Basis berada di sekitar {3}, tempat resistor {4} ke emitor mengambil {5} lagi — jadi resistor {6} harus membawa keduanya, dan mampu selama kapasitor tetap di atas sekitar <b>{7}</b>.`,"From full, that lasts about <b>{0}</b>. Below it, the base current falls away, the transistor is no longer fully on, and the LED fades; it is out after about <b>{1}</b>.":`Dari penuh, itu bertahan sekitar <b>{0}</b>. Di bawahnya, arus basis berkurang, transistor tidak lagi aktif penuh, dan LED meredup; padam setelah sekitar <b>{1}</b>.`,"Now: the capacitor has <b>{0}</b>; the base gets {1} and the LED {2}.":`Sekarang: kapasitor bertegangan <b>{0}</b>; basis mendapat {1} dan LED {2}.`,"Double the capacitance, double the time. Without the {0} the last trickle of base current would keep the LED glowing dimly for a minute or more: it makes the transistor let go cleanly. Real timers add a second transistor, or use a timer chip like the {1}, so the light snaps off instead of fading.":`Dua kali kapasitansi, dua kali waktu. Tanpa resistor {0}, sisa arus basis terakhir akan membuat LED menyala redup selama satu menit atau lebih: resistor itu membuat transistor melepas dengan bersih. Pewaktu sungguhan menambahkan transistor kedua, atau memakai cip pewaktu seperti {1}, agar lampu padam seketika alih-alih meredup.`,"fills the capacitor":`mengisi kapasitor`,"{0} · to the base, {1} · base to emitter, {2} · for the LED":`{0} · ke basis, {1} · basis ke emitor, {2} · untuk LED`,"BC547 transistor":`Transistor BC547`,"on · held":`menyala · ditahan`,"on · {0} left":`menyala · sisa {0}`,"Reading the code":`Membaca kode`,"{0}. Reading<br />the code":`{0}. Membaca<br />kode`,"Reading a capacitor":`Membaca kapasitor`,"Small ceramic capacitors carry a three-digit code: two digits, then how many zeros follow, in picofarads. {0} is {1} and four zeros: {2}, or {3}. Electrolytics simply print their value, with a stripe by the − leg.":`Kapasitor keramik kecil memiliki kode tiga digit: dua digit, lalu berapa nol yang mengikuti, dalam pikofarad. {0} berarti {1} dan empat nol: {2}, atau {3}. Kapasitor elektrolit cukup mencetak nilainya, dengan garis di dekat kaki −.`,"Two digits, then the number of zeros":`Dua digit, lalu jumlah nol`,"The answer is in picofarads (pF)":`Hasilnya dalam pikofarad (pF)`,"Electrolytics: the stripe marks −":`Elektrolit: garis menandai −`,Ceramic:`Keramik`,"Click it to change<br />the code.":`Klik untuk mengganti<br />kodenya.`,Electrolytic:`Elektrolit`,"Value printed on it,<br />stripe by the − leg.":`Nilai tercetak padanya,<br />garis di dekat kaki −.`,Zeros:`Nol`,"Two digits, then that many zeros, in picofarads:":`Dua digit, lalu nol sebanyak itu, dalam pikofarad:`,"Picofarads are tiny, so the answer is usually given in bigger units:":`Pikofarad sangat kecil, jadi hasilnya biasanya dinyatakan dalam satuan yang lebih besar:`,"The big blue electrolytic needs no code: {0} is printed on it, with its voltage limit, {1}, and a stripe down the − side. Electrolytics must go in the right way round; ceramics don’t mind.":`Kapasitor elektrolit biru yang besar tidak butuh kode: {0} tercetak padanya, beserta batas tegangannya, {1}, dan garis di sisi −. Elektrolit harus dipasang dengan arah yang benar; keramik tidak peduli.`,"Two more things you may see on a ceramic: a letter after the code for its tolerance (J ±{0}, K ±{1}, M ±{2}: “104K”), and a third digit of {3} or {4}, which means divide instead of adding zeros ({5} is {6}).":`Dua hal lagi yang mungkin kamu lihat pada keramik: huruf setelah kode untuk toleransinya (J ±{0}, K ±{1}, M ±{2}: “104K”), dan digit ketiga {3} atau {4}, yang berarti membagi alih-alih menambah nol ({5} berarti {6}).`,"ceramic · {0}":`keramik · {0}`,"either way round":`arah mana pun`,electrolytic:`elektrolit`,"+ to +, stripe to −":`+ ke +, garis ke −`,"Ceramic capacitor":`Kapasitor keramik`,"code {0} · {1}":`kode {0} · {1}`,"Electrolytic capacitor":`Kapasitor elektrolit`,"Push to light":`Tekan untuk menyala`,"{0}. Push to<br />light":`{0}. Tekan untuk<br />menyala`,"A push button":`Tombol tekan`,"A push button joins two wires only while you hold it down. Let go and a spring pops it back up, opening a gap in the circuit. That makes it momentary: it is on for exactly as long as you press.":`Tombol tekan menghubungkan dua kabel hanya selama kamu menahannya. Lepaskan dan pegas mendorongnya kembali, membuka celah di rangkaian. Itu membuatnya sesaat: menyala tepat selama kamu menekannya.`,"Hold the button down in the scene":`Tahan tombol di dalam adegan`,"Pressed, the loop is complete":`Saat ditekan, lingkaran lengkap`,"Let go, and the gap stops everything":`Lepaskan, dan celahnya menghentikan semuanya`,"Hold it down<br />to light the LED.":`Tahan untuk<br />menyalakan LED.`,"Lit only while<br />the button is down.":`Menyala hanya saat<br />tombol ditekan.`,"With the button up there is a gap in the loop. Air doesn’t conduct, so no current flows anywhere:":`Saat tombol tidak ditekan, ada celah di lingkaran. Udara tidak menghantarkan, jadi tidak ada arus yang mengalir di mana pun:`,"With no current the resistor and the LED drop nothing, so the whole {0} sits across the button’s open contacts.":`Tanpa arus, resistor dan LED tidak menurunkan apa pun, jadi seluruh {0} berada pada kontak tombol yang terbuka.`,"A current needs a complete loop. Break it anywhere — on the + side or the − side — and everything stops.":`Arus butuh lingkaran yang lengkap. Putuskan di mana saja — di sisi + atau sisi − — dan semuanya berhenti.`,"momentary, normally open":`sesaat, biasanya terbuka`,"Pressed, the button is just a piece of wire: the loop is complete, and Ohm’s law gives the current as before:":`Saat ditekan, tombol hanyalah sepotong kabel: lingkarannya lengkap, dan hukum Ohm memberi arusnya seperti sebelumnya:`,"Let go and see what happens to it.":`Lepaskan dan lihat apa yang terjadi padanya.`,"The current is the same all the way round the loop: the parts share out the voltage, but none of them uses up current.":`Arusnya sama di sepanjang lingkaran: komponen-komponen berbagi tegangan, tapi tidak ada yang menghabiskan arus.`,pressed:`ditekan`,"Slide switch":`Sakelar geser`,"{0}. Slide<br />switch":`{0}. Sakelar<br />geser`,"A switch that chooses":`Sakelar yang memilih`,"A slide switch stays where you put it. This one has three legs: the middle one (the common) is joined to the left leg or the right leg, depending on the slider — so it sends the current down one path or the other.":`Sakelar geser tetap di posisi yang kamu pilih. Yang ini punya tiga kaki: kaki tengah (bersama) terhubung ke kaki kiri atau kaki kanan, tergantung penggesernya — jadi ia mengirim arus ke satu jalur atau jalur lainnya.`,"Click the switch to slide it across":`Klik sakelar untuk menggesernya`,"The middle leg joins one side or the other":`Kaki tengah terhubung ke satu sisi atau sisi lainnya`,"Red on the left, green on the right":`Merah di kiri, hijau di kanan`,"Slide Switch":`Sakelar geser`,"Click it to slide<br />it across.":`Klik untuk<br />menggesernya.`,"On the right-hand<br />path.":`Di jalur<br />kanan.`,"On the left-hand<br />path.":`Di jalur<br />kiri.`,Slider:`Penggeser`,Left:`Kiri`,"The middle leg joins the left leg: the red LED’s path.":`Kaki tengah terhubung ke kaki kiri: jalur LED merah.`,Right:`Kanan`,"The middle leg joins the right leg: the green LED’s path.":`Kaki tengah terhubung ke kaki kanan: jalur LED hijau.`,left:`kiri`,"Only one path is ever complete. Through the red LED:":`Hanya satu jalur yang lengkap pada satu waktu. Melalui LED merah:`,"The other path has a gap at the switch, so it carries nothing.":`Jalur lainnya punya celah di sakelar, jadi tidak membawa apa pun.`,"Electricians call this a changeover switch; datasheets say SPDT — single pole, double throw: one common contact, two places to send it.":`Teknisi listrik menyebutnya sakelar tukar; lembar data menyebutnya SPDT — satu kutub, dua posisi: satu kontak bersama, dua tempat tujuan.`,"changeover · slider left":`sakelar tukar · penggeser kiri`,"Red and green LEDs":`LED merah dan hijau`,"{0} and {1}":`{0} dan {1}`,right:`kanan`,"Only one path is ever complete. Through the green LED:":`Hanya satu jalur yang lengkap pada satu waktu. Melalui LED hijau:`,"changeover · slider right":`sakelar tukar · penggeser kanan`,"AND & OR":`AND & OR`,"{0}. AND<br />& OR":`{0}. AND<br />& OR`,"AND and OR":`AND dan OR`,"Two switches in series must both be on for current to get through: that is AND. Side by side, in parallel, either one is enough: that is OR. The same two decisions sit inside every computer.":`Dua sakelar seri harus sama-sama aktif agar arus bisa lewat: itulah AND (DAN). Bersebelahan, paralel, salah satu saja sudah cukup: itulah OR (ATAU). Dua keputusan yang sama ini ada di dalam setiap komputer.`,"In series: S1 AND S2":`Seri: S1 AND S2`,"In parallel: S1 OR S2":`Paralel: S1 OR S2`,"Click the switches to flip them":`Klik sakelar untuk memindahkannya`,"Click it to flip it.<br />Right is on.":`Klik untuk memindahkannya.<br />Kanan berarti aktif.`,"Lights when the<br />current gets through.":`Menyala saat<br />arus lewat.`,"S1 on":`S1 aktif`,"S2 on":`S2 aktif`,Wiring:`Rangkaian`,"One after the other: both must be on (AND).":`Satu setelah yang lain: keduanya harus aktif (AND).`,"Side by side: either one will do (OR).":`Bersebelahan: salah satu sudah cukup (OR).`,"Every way the two switches can be, and what the LED does:":`Semua kemungkinan posisi kedua sakelar, dan apa yang dilakukan LED:`,"Series · AND":`Seri · AND`,"Parallel · OR":`Paralel · OR`,dark:`padam`,"{t0}lit</b>":`{t0}menyala</b>`,"In series the current must pass through S1 <i>and then</i> S2: one gap anywhere stops it.":`Dalam seri arus harus melewati S1 <i>lalu</i> S2: satu celah di mana saja menghentikannya.`,"Swap the switches for transistors and these are the AND and OR gates that computers are built from.":`Ganti sakelar dengan transistor dan inilah gerbang AND dan OR yang menyusun komputer.`,"S1 · off":`S1 · 0`,"S2 · off":`S2 · 0`,"Slide switches":`Sakelar geser`,"{0} · in series":`{0} · seri`,"S1 · on":`S1 · 1`,"S2 · on":`S2 · 1`,"In parallel the current has two ways round: if either switch is closed, it gets through.":`Dalam paralel arus punya dua jalur: jika salah satu sakelar tertutup, arus lewat.`,"{0} · in parallel":`{0} · paralel`,"Two-way switch":`Sakelar dua arah`,"{0}. Two-way<br />switch":`{0}. Sakelar<br />dua arah`,"The landing light":`Lampu tangga`,"A light on the stairs can be switched from the top and from the bottom. Two changeover switches are joined by two wires, the travellers: the light is on when both switches point the same way, so flipping either one changes it.":`Lampu di tangga bisa dinyalakan dari atas dan dari bawah. Dua sakelar tukar dihubungkan dengan dua kabel penghubung: lampu menyala saat kedua sakelar menunjuk ke arah yang sama, jadi memindahkan salah satunya mengubah lampu.`,"Two changeover switches":`Dua sakelar tukar`,"Two travellers between them":`Dua kabel penghubung di antaranya`,"Either switch turns the light on or off":`Salah satu sakelar menyalakan atau mematikan lampu`,"Switch {0}":`Sakelar {0}`,"Upstairs. Click<br />it to flip it.":`Di atas. Klik untuk<br />memindahkannya.`,"Landing Light":`Lampu tangga`,"On when both switches<br />point the same way.":`Menyala saat kedua sakelar<br />menunjuk ke arah yang sama.`,"Downstairs. Click<br />it to flip it.":`Di bawah. Klik untuk<br />memindahkannya.`,"The light is on when both switches pick the same traveller:":`Lampu menyala saat kedua sakelar memilih kabel penghubung yang sama:`,Light:`Lampu`,"Flipping either switch moves the current to the other traveller — and away from the one the other switch is waiting on — so every flip changes the light.":`Memindahkan salah satu sakelar mengalihkan arus ke kabel penghubung lainnya — menjauh dari kabel yang ditunggu sakelar satunya —, jadi setiap perpindahan mengubah lampu.`,"Mathematicians call this “equals” (or XNOR). Real stair lights work exactly this way, with mains switches. (In Britain they are called two-way switches; in North America, confusingly, three-way.)":`Ahli matematika menyebutnya “sama dengan” (atau XNOR). Lampu tangga sungguhan bekerja persis seperti ini, dengan sakelar listrik rumah. (Di Inggris disebut two-way switch; di Amerika Utara, membingungkan, three-way.)`,traveller:`kabel penghubung`,light:`lampu`,"{0} · left and right":`{0} · kiri dan kanan`,"the landing light":`lampu tangga`,"{0} · two of them travellers":`{0} · dua di antaranya kabel penghubung`,"{0} · right and right":`{0} · kanan dan kanan`,"{0} · left and left":`{0} · kiri dan kiri`,"Current control":`Pengendalian arus`,"{0}. Current<br />control":`{0}. Pengendalian<br />arus`,"A small current controls a big one":`Arus kecil mengendalikan arus besar`,"A transistor has three legs: collector, base and emitter. The small current into its base controls the much bigger one that can flow from its collector to its emitter. Turn the knob to change the base current and watch the LED’s current follow it on the chart — about {0} times as big — until the transistor is fully on.":`Transistor punya tiga kaki: kolektor, basis, dan emitor. Arus kecil yang masuk ke basisnya mengendalikan arus yang jauh lebih besar yang bisa mengalir dari kolektor ke emitornya. Putar kenop untuk mengubah arus basis dan lihat arus LED mengikutinya di grafik — sekitar {0} kali lebih besar — sampai transistor aktif penuh.`,"Drag around the knob to set the base current":`Seret mengelilingi kenop untuk mengatur arus basis`,"Collector current ≈ {0} × base current":`Arus kolektor ≈ {0} × arus basis`,"The chart: one current following the other":`Grafik: satu arus mengikuti yang lain`,Transistor:`Transistor`,"Collector, base, emitter:<br />C · B · E.":`Kolektor, basis, emitor:<br />C · B · E.`,"Drag around the knob<br />to set the base current.":`Seret mengelilingi kenop<br />untuk mengatur arus basis.`,"On the collector side:<br />the big current.":`Di sisi kolektor:<br />arus yang besar.`,"Current gain":`Penguatan arus`,"switched off":`mati`,"× {0}: amplifying":`× {0}: menguatkan`,"saturated: fully on":`jenuh: aktif penuh`,"base current":`arus basis`,"collector current":`arus kolektor`,"The pot is at {0}; with the {1}, the base current is":`Potensiometer berada di {0}; dengan resistor {1}, arus basisnya adalah`,"The transistor lets through about {0} times that — its gain, β:":`Transistor melewatkan sekitar {0} kali lipat — penguatannya, β:`,"That is below what the LED and its {0} allow, so the transistor sets the current: double the base current and the LED’s doubles too. On the chart, the dot is on the sloping line.":`Itu di bawah yang diizinkan LED dan resistor {0}-nya, jadi transistorlah yang menentukan arus: gandakan arus basis dan arus LED juga berlipat dua. Di grafik, titiknya berada di garis miring.`,"Why the {0}? Turned right up, the pot is {1} — without it the base would take far too much current. And the pot is a “log” one, like a volume knob: each bit of turn changes its resistance by about the same factor, so the current climbs steadily as you turn it.":`Mengapa {0}? Diputar penuh, potensiometer bernilai {1} — tanpanya basis akan mengambil arus terlalu besar. Dan potensiometernya jenis “logaritmik”, seperti kenop volume: setiap putaran sedikit mengubah hambatannya dengan faktor yang kurang lebih sama, jadi arus naik secara merata saat kamu memutarnya.`,"pot {0}":`pot. {0}`,"NPN · collector, base, emitter":`NPN · kolektor, basis, emitor`,"{0} log · now {1}":`{0} log · sekarang {1}`,"{0} · for the base, {1} · for the LED":`{0} · untuk basis, {1} · untuk LED`,"{0} in → {1} out":`{0} → {1}`,saturated:`jenuh`,"But the LED and its {0} only allow {1}, so that is all it gets: the transistor is <i>saturated</i>, fully on, and turning the knob further changes nothing. On the chart, the line has gone flat.":`Tapi LED dan resistor {0}-nya hanya mengizinkan {1}, jadi hanya itu yang didapatnya: transistor <i>jenuh</i>, aktif penuh, dan memutar kenop lebih jauh tidak mengubah apa pun. Di grafik, garisnya mendatar.`,"A current switch":`Sakelar arus`,"{0}. Current<br />switch":`{0}. Sakelar<br />arus`,"A switch worked by current":`Sakelar yang digerakkan arus`,"Give the base more current than the LED could ever use and the transistor is simply on: a switch, worked by current. Here the button sends about {0} into the base — and the LED gets about {1} times that.":`Beri basis arus lebih besar daripada yang mungkin dipakai LED dan transistor langsung aktif: sakelar yang digerakkan arus. Di sini tombol mengirim sekitar {0} ke basis — dan LED mendapat sekitar {1} kali lipatnya.`,"Base current switches the collector current":`Arus basis mensakelar arus kolektor`,"A tiny current controls a bigger one":`Arus mungil mengendalikan arus yang lebih besar`,"Hold it down to send<br />current into the base.":`Tahan untuk mengirim<br />arus ke basis.`,"The base drops about {0}, so the {1} lets this much into it:":`Basis menurunkan sekitar {0}, jadi resistor {1} melewatkan arus sebesar ini ke dalamnya:`,"A BC547 can pass about {0} times its base current:":`BC547 bisa melewatkan sekitar {0} kali arus basisnya:`,"But the LED and its {0} only allow":`Tapi LED dan resistor {0}-nya hanya mengizinkan`,"So the transistor is fully on — <i>saturated</i> — and works as a switch: {0} in, {1} out, about {2} times as much.":`Jadi transistor aktif penuh — <i>jenuh</i> — dan bekerja sebagai sakelar: {0} masuk, {1} keluar, sekitar {2} kali lebih besar.`,"{0} · for the LED":`{0} · untuk LED`,"{0} · for the base":`{0} · untuk basis`,"feeds the base":`memberi arus ke basis`,"{0}. Current<br />gain":`{0}. Penguatan<br />arus`,"Between off and fully on, a transistor amplifies: the collector current is about {0} times the base current, so halving one halves the other. Push in enough base current, though, and it can’t go any higher — it is saturated.":`Di antara mati dan aktif penuh, transistor menguatkan: arus kolektor sekitar {0} kali arus basis, jadi jika yang satu menjadi separuh, yang lain juga. Tapi beri arus basis yang cukup besar, dan arusnya tidak bisa naik lagi — transistor jenuh.`,"Click the base resistor to change it":`Klik resistor basis untuk menggantinya`,"Too much base current: saturated":`Arus basis terlalu besar: jenuh`,"Multiplies the base<br />current by about {0}.":`Mengalikan arus basis<br />sekitar {0} kali.`,"Base Resistor":`Resistor basis`,"Click it to change<br />the base current.":`Klik untuk mengubah<br />arus basis.`,"Its current follows<br />the base current.":`Arusnya mengikuti<br />arus basis.`,"Base resistor":`Resistor basis`,"About {0} into the base: the LED gets {1}.":`Sekitar {0} ke basis: LED mendapat {1}.`,"About {0} into the base: the LED gets {1} (saturated).":`Sekitar {0} ke basis: LED mendapat {1} (jenuh).`,"Into the base:":`Ke basis:`,"The transistor multiplies it by its gain, β:":`Transistor mengalikannya dengan penguatannya, β:`,"That is below the LED’s limit, so the transistor sets the current: it is amplifying.":`Itu di bawah batas LED, jadi transistorlah yang menentukan arus: ia sedang menguatkan.`,"This is how a transistor amplifies: a small, changing current at the base becomes a big copy of it at the collector. Real gains vary a lot, though: two BC547s off the same reel can differ by two or three times (anywhere from about {0} to {1}), which is why good circuits are designed not to depend on the exact number.":`Beginilah transistor menguatkan: arus kecil yang berubah-ubah di basis menjadi salinan besar di kolektor. Tapi penguatan sungguhan sangat bervariasi: dua BC547 dari gulungan yang sama bisa berbeda dua atau tiga kali (di mana saja antara sekitar {0} dan {1}), itulah sebabnya rangkaian yang baik dirancang agar tidak bergantung pada angka pastinya.`,"gain about {0}":`penguatan sekitar {0}`,"More than the LED’s {0} allows ({1}), so it gets {2}: the transistor is saturated, fully on, and more base current changes nothing.":`Lebih dari yang diizinkan {0} LED ({1}), jadi LED mendapat {2}: transistor jenuh, aktif penuh, dan arus basis yang lebih besar tidak mengubah apa pun.`,"NPN and PNP":`NPN dan PNP`,"{0}. NPN and<br />PNP":`{0}. NPN dan<br />PNP`,"Transistors come in two kinds. An NPN, like the BC547, sits between the LED and −, and switches on when current flows into its base. A PNP, like the BC557, is its mirror image: it sits between + and the LED, and switches on when current flows out of its base, down towards −.":`Transistor ada dua jenis. NPN, seperti BC547, berada di antara LED dan −, dan aktif saat arus mengalir masuk ke basisnya. PNP, seperti BC557, adalah bayangan cerminnya: berada di antara + dan LED, dan aktif saat arus mengalir keluar dari basisnya, ke arah −.`,"Click the transistor to swap NPN and PNP":`Klik transistor untuk menukar NPN dan PNP`,"Watch which way the base current flows":`Lihat ke arah mana arus basis mengalir`,"Click it to swap<br />NPN and PNP.":`Klik untuk menukar<br />NPN dan PNP.`,"Hold it down to<br />switch it on.":`Tahan untuk<br />mengaktifkannya.`,"Lit by either kind,<br />wired its own way.":`Dinyalakan oleh keduanya,<br />masing-masing dengan caranya.`,"NPN · BC547":`NPN · BC547`,"Between the LED and −. Current flows into its base, from +.":`Di antara LED dan −. Arus mengalir masuk ke basisnya, dari +.`,"PNP · BC557":`PNP · BC557`,"Between + and the LED. Current flows out of its base, to −.":`Di antara + dan LED. Arus mengalir keluar dari basisnya, ke −.`,"The two kinds, side by side:":`Kedua jenis, berdampingan:`,"Its emitter goes to":`Emitornya ke`,"It sits":`Posisinya`,"between the LED and −":`di antara LED dan −`,"between + and the LED":`di antara + dan LED`,"Its base current":`Arus basisnya`,"flows in":`masuk`,"flows out":`keluar`,"Switched on by":`Diaktifkan dengan`,"pulling the base up, towards +":`menarik basis naik, ke arah +`,"pulling the base down, towards −":`menarik basis turun, ke arah −`,"Its main current":`Arus utamanya`,"collector → emitter":`kolektor → emitor`,"emitter → collector":`emitor → kolektor`,"Either way the sums are the same. The base sits about {0} above the emitter (−), so the {1} carries":`Bagaimanapun, hitungannya sama. Basis berada sekitar {0} di atas emitor (−), jadi resistor {1} membawa`,"{0} times that is more than the LED and its {1} allow, so the transistor is fully on and the LED gets <b>{2}</b>.":`{0} kali lipatnya lebih dari yang diizinkan LED dan resistor {1}-nya, jadi transistor aktif penuh dan LED mendapat <b>{2}</b>.`,"The arrow on the emitter in the symbol shows which way the current flows: out of an NPN, into a PNP. A way to remember it: NPN — “Not Pointing iN”.":`Panah pada emitor di simbolnya menunjukkan arah arus: keluar dari NPN, masuk ke PNP.`,"Either way the sums are the same. The base sits about {0} below the emitter (+), so the {1} carries":`Bagaimanapun, hitungannya sama. Basis berada sekitar {0} di bawah emitor (+), jadi resistor {1} membawa`,"BC557 transistor":`Transistor BC557`,"PNP · collector, base, emitter":`PNP · kolektor, basis, emitor`,"pulls the base down":`menarik basis turun`,"Touch switch":`Sakelar sentuh`,"{0}. Touch<br />switch":`{0}. Sakelar<br />sentuh`,"A touch switch":`Sakelar sentuh`,"Your skin conducts, just badly: across a touch pad, a few microamps get through your finger. One transistor turns that into a faint glow. Two in a row — a Darlington pair — multiply their gains, and the same touch lights the LED fully.":`Kulitmu menghantarkan listrik, hanya saja buruk: melewati bantalan sentuh, beberapa mikroampere mengalir melalui jarimu. Satu transistor mengubahnya menjadi pendar redup. Dua berderet — pasangan Darlington — saling mengalikan penguatannya, dan sentuhan yang sama menyalakan LED sepenuhnya.`,"Hold your finger on the pad":`Tahan jarimu di atas bantalan`,"One transistor: {0} × the current":`Satu transistor: {0} × arusnya`,"Two: {0} × {1} = {2} ×":`Dua: {0} × {1} = {2} ×`,"Click it to add<br />a second one.":`Klik untuk menambahkan<br />yang kedua.`,"Touch Pad":`Bantalan sentuh`,"Hold your finger<br />down on it.":`Tahan jarimu<br />di atasnya.`,"Faint with one transistor,<br />bright with two.":`Redup dengan satu transistor,<br />terang dengan dua.`,"A gain of about {0}.":`Penguatan sekitar {0}.`,"Two (Darlington)":`Dua (Darlington)`,"The first feeds the second: about {0} × {1} = {2}.":`Yang pertama memberi arus ke yang kedua: sekitar {0} × {1} = {2}.`,"touch me":`sentuh aku`,"Through about {0} of finger, on {1}:":`Melalui sekitar {0} jari, pada {1}:`,"One transistor multiplies that by {0}:":`Satu transistor mengalikannya {0} kali:`,"{0} × {1} = <b>{2}</b> — a faint glow":`{0} × {1} = <b>{2}</b> — pendar redup`,"In a Darlington pair the first transistor’s output is the second one’s input, so the gains multiply. Its base drops twice as much ({0}):":`Dalam pasangan Darlington, keluaran transistor pertama adalah masukan transistor kedua, jadi penguatannya saling dikalikan. Basisnya menurunkan dua kali lipat ({0}):`,"Far more than the LED needs: the pair is fully on and the LED gets <b>{0}</b>. (A little less than one transistor would give it: a Darlington can’t pull its collector right down, but keeps about {1} for itself — the second one’s base-emitter drop plus the first’s own.)":`Jauh lebih besar dari yang dibutuhkan LED: pasangan itu aktif penuh dan LED mendapat <b>{0}</b>. (Sedikit lebih kecil daripada yang akan diberikan satu transistor: Darlington tidak bisa menarik kolektornya sampai bawah, tapi menyisakan sekitar {1} untuk dirinya — penurunan basis-emitor transistor kedua ditambah milik transistor pertama.)`,"The {0} keeps the base safe if the pad is ever shorted by a wire instead of a finger.":`Resistor {0} menjaga basis tetap aman jika bantalan suatu saat terhubung singkat oleh kabel alih-alih jari.`,"your finger":`jarimu`,"Touch pad":`Bantalan sentuh`,"about {0} through a finger":`sekitar {0} melalui jari`,touching:`menyentuh`,"BC547 transistors":`Transistor BC547`,"{0} · a Darlington pair":`{0} · pasangan Darlington`,"Turn it round: NOT":`Balikkan: NOT`,"{0}. Turn it<br />round: NOT":`{0}. Balikkan:<br />NOT`,"NOT: press to switch off":`NOT: tekan untuk mematikan`,"Put the transistor beside the LED instead of in line with it, and it works the other way round. When the base gets current, the transistor opens an easy path past the LED and takes the current for itself: press the button and the LED goes out.":`Pasang transistor di samping LED alih-alih seri dengannya, dan ia bekerja sebaliknya. Saat basis mendapat arus, transistor membuka jalur mudah di samping LED dan mengambil arus untuk dirinya sendiri: tekan tombol dan LED padam.`,"The transistor takes the LED’s current":`Transistor mengambil arus LED`,"Button on, LED off: NOT":`Tombol ditekan, LED padam: NOT`,"Beside the LED, not<br />in line with it.":`Di samping LED,<br />bukan seri dengannya.`,"Hold it down: the<br />LED goes out.":`Tahan: LED<br />padam.`,"Lit until the transistor<br />takes its current.":`Menyala sampai transistor<br />mengambil arusnya.`,"The button and the LED, every way round:":`Tombol dan LED, dalam semua keadaan:`,Button:`Tombol`,up:`dilepas`,"Pressed, the base gets {0} and the transistor draws {1} through the {2}. That drops":`Saat ditekan, basis mendapat {0} dan transistor menarik {1} melalui resistor {2}. Itu menurunkan`,"leaving less than the {0} the LED needs, so it goes out.":`menyisakan kurang dari {0} yang dibutuhkan LED, jadi LED padam.`,"The output is the opposite of the input: a NOT gate, or inverter. With the AND and OR from the switches lesson, that is enough to build any logic. Put a NOT after an AND and you have a NAND gate: copied enough times, NANDs alone can build a whole computer.":`Keluarannya kebalikan dari masukannya: gerbang NOT, atau inverter. Bersama AND dan OR dari pelajaran sakelar, itu cukup untuk membangun logika apa pun. Pasang NOT setelah AND dan kamu mendapat gerbang NAND: jika disalin cukup banyak, NAND saja bisa membangun sebuah komputer utuh.`,"beside the LED":`di samping LED`,"Light sensor":`Sensor cahaya`,"{0}. Light<br />sensor":`{0}. Sensor<br />cahaya`,"A resistor that sees light":`Resistor yang bisa melihat cahaya`,"A light-dependent resistor (LDR) is made of a material that conducts better the more light falls on it. In bright light it is about {0}; in the dark it climbs to a megohm. Dim the lamp and watch the meter.":`Resistor yang bergantung pada cahaya (LDR) terbuat dari bahan yang makin baik menghantarkan saat makin banyak cahaya mengenainya. Dalam cahaya terang nilainya sekitar {0}; dalam gelap naik sampai satu megaohm. Redupkan lampu dan perhatikan alat ukurnya.`,"More light, less resistance":`Makin banyak cahaya, makin kecil hambatan`,"Click the lamp to change its brightness":`Klik lampu untuk mengubah terangnya`,"The meter reads the LDR, set to Ω":`Alat ukur membaca LDR, pada mode Ω`,"Desk Lamp":`Lampu meja`,"Click it to make it<br />brighter or dimmer.":`Klik untuk membuatnya<br />lebih terang atau lebih redup.`,"Light Sensor":`Sensor cahaya`,"Less resistance the<br />more light it gets.":`Makin kecil hambatannya, makin<br />banyak cahaya yang diterimanya.`,"Set to Ω, it reads<br />the LDR.":`Pada mode Ω, membaca<br />LDR.`,"Lamp brightness":`Kecerahan lampu`,"Each step in brightness divides the resistance by the same amount, so it is easiest to see on a scale of tens:":`Setiap tingkat kecerahan membagi hambatan dengan faktor yang sama, jadi paling mudah dilihat dalam skala puluhan:`,dusk:`senja`,"dim room":`ruangan redup`,"bright lamp":`lampu terang`,"At {0} the LDR measures":`Pada {0}, LDR terukur`,"Light knocks electrons loose in the cadmium sulphide track (the orange zig-zag on its face), and more free electrons means less resistance. Cadmium is poisonous, so many countries now limit LDRs; newer designs use photodiodes or phototransistors, which do the same job faster.":`Cahaya melepaskan elektron di jalur kadmium sulfida (zig-zag oranye di permukaannya), dan lebih banyak elektron bebas berarti hambatan lebih kecil. Kadmium beracun, jadi banyak negara kini membatasi LDR; rancangan yang lebih baru memakai fotodioda atau fototransistor, yang melakukan tugas yang sama lebih cepat.`,"LDR · {0}":`LDR · {0}`,"meter off":`alat ukur mati`,"Light sensor (LDR)":`Sensor cahaya (LDR)`,"{0} at {1}":`{0} pada {1}`,"Desk lamp":`Lampu meja`,"{0} bright":`kecerahan {0}`,"set to Ω":`pada mode Ω`,"Test probes":`Probe uji`,"one on each leg":`satu di setiap kaki`,"Night light":`Lampu tidur`,"{0}. Night<br />light":`{0}. Lampu<br />tidur`,"A light that comes on in the dark":`Lampu yang menyala saat gelap`,"Put the LDR at the bottom of a voltage divider and feed its middle to a transistor. In the light the LDR’s low resistance pulls the middle down, and the transistor stays off. As it gets dark the middle rises, the base gets current, and the LED comes on by itself.":`Pasang LDR di bagian bawah pembagi tegangan dan hubungkan titik tengahnya ke transistor. Saat terang, hambatan LDR yang rendah menarik titik tengah turun, dan transistor tetap mati. Saat mulai gelap, titik tengah naik, basis mendapat arus, dan LED menyala sendiri.`,"The LDR and {0} make a divider":`LDR dan {0} membentuk pembagi`,"The divider feeds the transistor’s base":`Pembagi memberi arus ke basis transistor`,"Click the lamp to dim it":`Klik lampu untuk meredupkannya`,"The daylight. Click<br />it to dim it.":`Cahaya siang. Klik<br />untuk meredupkannya.`,"Bottom of a divider<br />with the {0}.":`Bagian bawah pembagi<br />dengan {0}.`,"Night Light":`Lampu tidur`,"Comes on when<br />it gets dark.":`Menyala saat<br />mulai gelap.`,"At {0} light the LDR is {1}. With the {2} above it, the middle of the divider would sit at":`Pada cahaya {0}, LDR bernilai {1}. Dengan {2} di atasnya, titik tengah pembagi akan berada di`,"Below the {0} or so the base needs, so almost no current flows into it and the LED stays dark.":`Di bawah sekitar {0} yang dibutuhkan basis, jadi hampir tidak ada arus yang masuk ke basis dan LED tetap padam.`,"The middle reaches the base’s {0} once the LDR rises to about {1} — at about {2} lamp brightness, as dusk falls. (A transistor doesn’t switch all at once, so the LED starts to glow a little before that.)":`Titik tengah mencapai {0} untuk basis begitu LDR naik ke sekitar {1} — pada kecerahan lampu sekitar {2}, saat senja tiba. (Transistor tidak mensakelar sekaligus, jadi LED mulai berpendar sedikit sebelum itu.)`,"Swap the {0} for a bigger resistor and the middle sits lower, so it waits until it is darker; a smaller one switches it on in brighter light. The next lessons use that to set the switching point.":`Ganti {0} dengan resistor yang lebih besar dan titik tengah berada lebih rendah, jadi ia menunggu sampai lebih gelap; resistor yang lebih kecil menyalakannya dalam cahaya yang lebih terang. Pelajaran berikutnya memakai ini untuk mengatur titik pensakelaran.`,"LDR {0}":`LDR {0}`,"bottom of the divider":`bagian bawah pembagi`,"switches the LED":`mensakelar LED`,"the night light":`lampu tidur`,"the daylight":`cahaya siang`,"Enough for the base: {0} flows into it, and the transistor lets {1} through the LED — as much as its {2} allows.":`Cukup untuk basis: {0} masuk ke basis, dan transistor melewatkan {1} melalui LED — sebanyak yang diizinkan resistor {2}-nya.`,"Just about enough for the base: a trickle flows into it, and the LED only glows faintly ({0}).":`Hampir cukup untuk basis: arus kecil masuk ke basis, dan LED hanya berpendar redup ({0}).`,"Temperature sensor":`Sensor suhu`,"{0}. Temperature<br />sensor":`{0}. Sensor<br />suhu`,"Sensing temperature":`Mendeteksi suhu`,"A thermistor is a resistor that changes with temperature. This one (an NTC) has less resistance the warmer it gets. In a divider with a {0} resistor that becomes a voltage: hold your finger on it and watch the meter climb as it warms.":`Termistor adalah resistor yang berubah karena suhu. Yang ini (NTC) hambatannya makin kecil saat makin hangat. Dalam pembagi dengan resistor {0}, itu menjadi tegangan: tahan jarimu di atasnya dan lihat alat ukur naik saat memanas.`,"Hold your finger on the thermistor":`Tahan jarimu di atas termistor`,"The meter reads the divider":`Alat ukur membaca pembagi`,"Warmer, less resistance, more volts":`Lebih hangat, hambatan lebih kecil, volt lebih besar`,Thermistor:`Termistor`,"Hold your finger<br />on it to warm it.":`Tahan jarimu di atasnya<br />untuk menghangatkannya.`,Voltmeter:`Voltmeter`,"Reads the voltage<br />across the {0}.":`Membaca tegangan<br />pada resistor {0}.`,"The fixed half of<br />the divider.":`Separuh pembagi<br />yang tetap.`,Temperature:`Suhu`,"An NTC thermistor’s resistance falls as it warms. This one is {0} at {1}; at {2} it is":`Hambatan termistor NTC turun saat menghangat. Termistor ini bernilai {0} pada {1}; pada {2} nilainya`,"It sits above a fixed {0}, and the meter reads the voltage across the {1}:":`Termistor berada di atas resistor tetap {0}, dan alat ukur membaca tegangan pada resistor {1}:`,Meter:`Alat ukur`,"A microcontroller reads that voltage and turns it back into a temperature: that is how a digital thermometer works. Around room temperature the voltage climbs fairly evenly, about {0} a degree, but further out the curve flattens (near boiling it is under {1} a degree), so it uses the thermistor’s formula or a look-up table rather than a straight line.":`Mikrokontroler membaca tegangan itu dan mengubahnya kembali menjadi suhu: begitulah termometer digital bekerja. Di sekitar suhu ruangan tegangannya naik cukup merata, sekitar {0} per derajat, tapi lebih jauh kurvanya mendatar (dekat titik didih kurang dari {1} per derajat), jadi ia memakai rumus termistor atau tabel alih-alih garis lurus.`,middle:`tengah`,"{0} at {1} · NTC":`{0} pada {1} · NTC`,"set to V":`pada mode V`,"Reed switch":`Sakelar reed`,"{0}. Reed<br />switch":`{0}. Sakelar<br />reed`,"A switch worked by a magnet":`Sakelar yang digerakkan magnet`,"A reed switch is two thin iron reeds sealed in a glass tube, almost touching. Bring a magnet close and it magnetises them: they pull together and close the circuit. Nothing touches the switch — which is why reed switches tell alarms when a door or window opens.":`Sakelar reed adalah dua bilah besi tipis yang tersegel dalam tabung kaca, hampir bersentuhan. Dekatkan magnet dan magnet itu memagnetisasinya: kedua bilah saling menarik dan menutup rangkaian. Tidak ada yang menyentuh sakelarnya — itulah sebabnya sakelar reed memberi tahu alarm saat pintu atau jendela terbuka.`,"Two reeds sealed in glass":`Dua bilah yang tersegel dalam kaca`,"Click the magnet to bring it close":`Klik magnet untuk mendekatkannya`,"Magnet near: the reeds close":`Magnet dekat: bilahnya menutup`,"Reed Switch":`Sakelar reed`,"Two iron reeds<br />in a glass tube.":`Dua bilah besi<br />dalam tabung kaca.`,"Lights when the<br />reeds close.":`Menyala saat<br />bilahnya menutup.`,Magnet:`Magnet`,"Click it to bring it<br />up to the switch.":`Klik untuk mendekatkannya<br />ke sakelar.`,"Magnet next to the switch":`Magnet di samping sakelar`,"Electrically, a reed switch is just a switch:":`Secara listrik, sakelar reed hanyalah sakelar:`,Reeds:`Bilah`,far:`jauh`,near:`dekat`,"Closed, the current is set by the {0} as usual:":`Saat tertutup, arusnya ditentukan oleh resistor {0} seperti biasa:`,"A door alarm puts the magnet on the door and the reed switch in the frame: open the door, the magnet moves away, the switch opens — and the alarm notices.":`Alarm pintu memasang magnet di pintu dan sakelar reed di kusen: buka pintunya, magnet menjauh, sakelar terbuka — dan alarm menyadarinya.`,"reed · open":`reed · terbuka`,"Bar magnet":`Magnet batang`,"on the bench":`di atas meja`,"reed · closed":`reed · tertutup`,"next to the switch":`di samping sakelar`,"Heat alarm":`Alarm panas`,"{0}. Heat<br />alarm":`{0}. Alarm<br />panas`,"A light that comes on when it gets warm":`Lampu yang menyala saat panas`,"The night light’s circuit, with the sensor moved to the top of the divider: a thermistor above a {0} resistor. As the thermistor warms, its resistance falls, the divider’s middle rises, and once it passes about {1} the transistor switches the LED on. Hold your finger on the thermistor — your skin is warmer than the room.":`Rangkaian lampu tidur, dengan sensornya dipindah ke bagian atas pembagi: termistor di atas resistor {0}. Saat termistor menghangat, hambatannya turun, titik tengah pembagi naik, dan begitu melewati sekitar {1}, transistor menyalakan LED. Tahan jarimu di atas termistor — kulitmu lebih hangat daripada ruangan.`,"Thermistor on top, {0} below":`Termistor di atas, {0} di bawah`,"Warm enough, the LED comes on":`Cukup hangat, LED menyala`,"Top of the divider.<br />Hold it to warm it.":`Bagian atas pembagi.<br />Tahan untuk menghangatkannya.`,"Alarm Light":`Lampu alarm`,"Comes on when<br />it gets warm.":`Menyala saat<br />mulai panas.`,"The fixed bottom<br />of the divider.":`Bagian bawah pembagi<br />yang tetap.`,"At {0} the thermistor is {1}. With the {2} below it, the middle of the divider would sit at":`Pada {0} termistor bernilai {1}. Dengan {2} di bawahnya, titik tengah pembagi akan berada di`,"The middle reaches {0} once the thermistor falls to about {1}, at about {2}. A transistor doesn’t switch all at once, so the LED starts to glow a few degrees before that:":`Titik tengah mencapai {0} begitu termistor turun ke sekitar {1}, pada sekitar {2}. Transistor tidak mensakelar sekaligus, jadi LED mulai berpendar beberapa derajat sebelumnya:`,Middle:`Tengah`,faint:`redup`,"In the night light the sensor is at the bottom of the divider, so it switches on as the sensor’s resistance rises. Here it is at the top, so it switches on as its resistance falls. Swap the thermistor and a fixed resistor round and you have a frost alarm, which comes on in the cold.":`Pada lampu tidur sensornya di bagian bawah pembagi, jadi menyala saat hambatan sensor naik. Di sini sensornya di atas, jadi menyala saat hambatannya turun. Tukar posisi termistor dan resistor tetap, dan kamu mendapat alarm beku, yang menyala saat dingin.`,"{0} at {1} · NTC, top of the divider":`{0} pada {1} · NTC, bagian atas pembagi`,"the alarm light":`lampu alarm`,"Enough for the base: {0} flows into it, and the transistor lets {1} through the LED.":`Cukup untuk basis: {0} masuk ke basis, dan transistor melewatkan {1} melalui LED.`,"Adjustable night light":`Lampu tidur yang bisa diatur`,"{0}. Adjustable<br />night light":`{0}. Lampu tidur<br />yang bisa diatur`,"Choosing when it switches":`Memilih kapan ia menyala`,"Real sensor circuits have a small adjustable resistor, a trimmer, to set exactly when they switch. Here a {0} trimmer and a {1} resistor make the top of the night light’s divider. Turn the trimmer up and the LDR has to get darker — its resistance higher — before the middle reaches {2} and the LED comes on.":`Rangkaian sensor sungguhan punya resistor kecil yang bisa diatur, trimpot, untuk menentukan dengan tepat kapan rangkaian itu mensakelar. Di sini trimpot {0} dan resistor {1} membentuk bagian atas pembagi lampu tidur. Naikkan trimpot dan LDR harus lebih gelap — hambatannya lebih tinggi — sebelum titik tengah mencapai {2} dan LED menyala.`,"Drag the trimmer’s screw to turn it":`Seret sekrup trimpot untuk memutarnya`,"More resistance on top: it waits for darker":`Hambatan lebih besar di atas: menunggu lebih gelap`,Trimmer:`Trimpot`,"Turn it to choose<br />how dark it waits for.":`Putar untuk memilih<br />seberapa gelap yang ditunggu.`,"The top of the divider is the {0} and the trimmer in series:":`Bagian atas pembagi adalah resistor {0} dan trimpot yang dirangkai seri:`,"The middle reaches the base’s {0} when the LDR is {1} ÷ {2} of that:":`Titik tengah mencapai {0} untuk basis saat LDR bernilai {1} ÷ {2} dari itu:`,"so the LED comes on below about <b>{0}</b> lamp brightness. Now, at {1}, the LDR is {2} and the middle sits at {3}: Enough for the base: {4} flows into it, and the transistor lets {5} through the LED.":`jadi LED menyala di bawah sekitar <b>{0}</b> kecerahan lampu. Sekarang, pada {1}, LDR bernilai {2} dan titik tengah berada di {3}: Cukup untuk basis: {4} masuk ke basis, dan transistor melewatkan {5} melalui LED.`,Top:`Atas`,"Comes on below":`Menyala di bawah`,"Why the {0}? Turned right down, the trimmer is {1}. Without the {2}, the base would then be joined straight to the {3}, and the current into it would destroy the transistor.":`Mengapa {0}? Diputar turun penuh, trimpot bernilai {1}. Tanpa {2}, basis akan langsung terhubung ke {3}, dan arus yang masuk akan merusak transistor.`,"{0}, set to {1}":`{0}, diatur ke {1}`,"so the LED comes on below about <b>{0}</b> lamp brightness. Now, at {1}, the LDR is {2} and the middle sits at {3}: Enough for the base: {4} flows into it, and the transistor lets {5} through the LED — as much as its {6} allows.":`jadi LED menyala di bawah sekitar <b>{0}</b> kecerahan lampu. Sekarang, pada {1}, LDR bernilai {2} dan titik tengah berada di {3}: Cukup untuk basis: {4} masuk ke basis, dan transistor melewatkan {5} melalui LED — sebanyak yang diizinkan resistor {6}-nya.`,"so the LED comes on below about <b>{0}</b> lamp brightness. Now, at {1}, the LDR is {2} and the middle sits at {3}: Just about enough for the base: a trickle flows into it, and the LED only glows faintly ({4}).":`jadi LED menyala di bawah sekitar <b>{0}</b> kecerahan lampu. Sekarang, pada {1}, LDR bernilai {2} dan titik tengah berada di {3}: Hampir cukup untuk basis: arus kecil masuk ke basis, dan LED hanya berpendar redup ({4}).`,"so the LED comes on below about <b>{0}</b> lamp brightness. Now, at {1}, the LDR is {2} and the middle sits at {3}: Below the {4} or so the base needs, so almost no current flows into it and the LED stays dark.":`jadi LED menyala di bawah sekitar <b>{0}</b> kecerahan lampu. Sekarang, pada {1}, LDR bernilai {2} dan titik tengah berada di {3}: Di bawah sekitar {4} yang dibutuhkan basis, jadi hampir tidak ada arus yang masuk ke basis dan LED tetap padam.`,"Hall-effect sensor":`Sensor efek Hall`,"{0}. Hall<br />sensor":`{0}. Sensor<br />Hall`,"Sensing a magnet with no moving parts":`Mendeteksi magnet tanpa bagian yang bergerak`,"A Hall-effect sensor is a chip with a thin slice of semiconductor inside. A current flows through the slice; a magnetic field across it pushes the moving charges to one side, making a tiny voltage, the Hall voltage. The chip amplifies that and, when it is big enough, switches its output on. Unlike the reed switch nothing moves, the chip needs power — and this kind only answers a south pole.":`Sensor efek Hall adalah cip berisi irisan tipis semikonduktor. Arus mengalir melalui irisan itu; medan magnet yang menembusnya mendorong muatan yang bergerak ke satu sisi, menghasilkan tegangan mungil, tegangan Hall. Cip menguatkannya dan, saat cukup besar, mengaktifkan keluarannya. Berbeda dengan sakelar reed, tidak ada yang bergerak, cipnya butuh daya — dan jenis ini hanya merespons kutub selatan.`,"Click the magnet: away, south or north towards the chip":`Klik magnet: jauh, atau kutub selatan atau utara menghadap cip`,"Three legs: power, ground and output":`Tiga kaki: daya, ground, dan keluaran`,"South pole at its printed face: the LED lights":`Kutub selatan di sisi tercetaknya: LED menyala`,"Hall Sensor":`Sensor Hall`,"Printed face to the<br />back, to the magnet.":`Sisi tercetak menghadap belakang,<br />ke arah magnet.`,"Lights when the<br />output switches on.":`Menyala saat<br />keluarannya aktif.`,"Click it: away, south<br />or north pole close.":`Klik: jauh, kutub selatan<br />atau utara dekat.`,Away:`Jauh`,"No field at the chip: its output is off.":`Tidak ada medan di cip: keluarannya mati.`,"South pole close":`Kutub selatan dekat`,"The south pole faces the chip’s printed face: the output switches on.":`Kutub selatan menghadap sisi tercetak cip: keluarannya aktif.`,"North pole close":`Kutub utara dekat`,"The field goes through the chip the other way: this kind ignores it.":`Medan menembus cip ke arah sebaliknya: jenis ini mengabaikannya.`,"output off":`keluaran mati`,Output:`Keluaran`,away:`jauh`,"south pole close":`kutub selatan dekat`,"<b>on</b>":`<b>aktif</b>`,"north pole close":`kutub utara dekat`,"The output is an <i>open drain</i>: switched on, it joins its pin to ground; off, it lets go. So the LED and its resistor go from + to the output, and the chip pulls their current through to −:":`Keluarannya <i>open drain</i>: saat aktif, ia menghubungkan pinnya ke ground; saat mati, ia melepasnya. Jadi LED dan resistornya dipasang dari + ke keluaran, dan cip menarik arusnya ke −:`,"The chip itself also draws a few milliamps all the time, from its power leg to ground, to run its sensor and amplifier — magnet or not.":`Cip itu sendiri juga menarik beberapa miliampere sepanjang waktu, dari kaki dayanya ke ground, untuk menjalankan sensor dan penguatnya — ada magnet atau tidak.`,"A reed switch closes for either pole. A Hall switch like this one is <i>unipolar</i>: only a south pole facing its printed side turns it on (there are also kinds that answer either pole, and kinds that measure the field’s strength). Phones use one to notice a flip cover closing, and brushless motors use them to know where their magnets are. Check the supply it needs: many popular ones (such as the A3144) want at least {0}, so on {1} use one made for low voltages.":`Sakelar reed menutup oleh kutub mana pun. Sakelar Hall seperti ini <i>unipolar</i>: hanya kutub selatan yang menghadap sisi tercetaknya yang mengaktifkannya (ada juga jenis yang merespons kedua kutub, dan jenis yang mengukur kekuatan medan). Ponsel memakai satu untuk mengetahui sampul lipat yang menutup, dan motor tanpa sikat memakainya untuk mengetahui letak magnetnya. Periksa catu daya yang dibutuhkannya: banyak yang populer (seperti A3144) butuh setidaknya {0}, jadi pada {1} pakailah yang dibuat untuk tegangan rendah.`,"Hall-effect switch":`Sakelar efek Hall`,"printed face to the back":`sisi tercetak menghadap belakang`,"output on":`keluaran aktif`,"south pole to the chip":`kutub selatan menghadap cip`,"north pole to the chip":`kutub utara menghadap cip`,"Scroll back":`Gulir mundur`,"Scroll on":`Gulir maju`,"Fold the chart away":`Lipat grafik`,"Lesson {0}":`Pelajaran {0}`,"{0} lessons":`{0} pelajaran`,"Loading fonts":`Memuat fon`,"Loading the 3D view":`Memuat tampilan 3D`,"Setting out the bench":`Menyiapkan meja kerja`,"Put the values back":`Kembalikan nilai awal`,Off:`Mati`,"Power off":`Daya mati`,"Power: on":`Nyalakan daya`,Space:`Spasi`,"Click a highlighted part to change it.":`Klik komponen yang disorot untuk mengubahnya.`,switch:`sakelar`,"Change:":`Ubah:`,"Battery · {0}":`Baterai · {0}`,"Pushes current out of its + end, round the circuit and back into its − end.":`Mendorong arus keluar dari ujung +, mengitari rangkaian, dan kembali ke ujung −.`,"Current through its thin filament heats it white-hot: the more current, the brighter.":`Arus yang melewati filamennya yang tipis memanaskannya sampai berpijar: makin besar arus, makin terang.`,"A gap you can open and close: click it to lift the blade out of its clip, or drop it back in.":`Celah yang bisa dibuka dan ditutup: klik untuk mengangkat bilahnya dari penjepit, atau memasukkannya kembali.`,"Drawing the lessons":`Menggambar pelajaran`,"Drawing the lessons · {0} / {1}":`Menggambar pelajaran · {0} / {1}`,Components:`Komponen`,"{0} in this circuit":`{0} di rangkaian ini`,"{0}/{1} done":`{0}/{1} selesai`,"DIGITAL MULTIMETER":`MULTIMETER DIGITAL`,"What this circuit is built from.":`Bahan penyusun rangkaian ini.`,"The maths":`Perhitungan`,"Power on":`Daya menyala`,"Power: off":`Matikan daya`,Close:`Tutup`,"Zoom to it":`Perbesar`,"Run to see it":`Jalankan untuk melihatnya`,"Click it in the scene to flip it":`Klik di adegan untuk memindahkannya`,Part:`Komponen`,"Two bare posts: whatever you lay across them becomes part of the circuit.":`Dua kutub terbuka: apa pun yang kamu letakkan di atasnya menjadi bagian rangkaian.`,"Copper wire":`Kawat tembaga`,"Copper lets current through more easily than almost anything: it is what wires are made of.":`Tembaga melewatkan arus lebih mudah daripada hampir semua bahan lain: dari itulah kabel dibuat.`,"Steel: a metal, so it conducts — not quite as well as copper, but plenty for an LED.":`Baja: logam, jadi menghantarkan — tidak sebaik tembaga, tapi lebih dari cukup untuk LED.`,"Graphite (the “lead” in a pencil) conducts, but resists a good deal more than metal.":`Grafit (“isi” pensil) menghantarkan, tapi jauh lebih menghambat daripada logam.`,"Lolly stick":`Stik es krim`,"Dry wood is an insulator: no current to speak of gets through.":`Kayu kering adalah isolator: hampir tidak ada arus yang lewat.`,"Rubber eraser":`Penghapus karet`,"Rubber is an excellent insulator — the reason tools have rubber handles.":`Karet adalah isolator yang sangat baik — itulah sebabnya perkakas punya pegangan karet.`,"Volt (V)":`Volt (V)`,"The push: the voltage drives the current round. More volts, a harder push.":`Dorongan: tegangan menggerakkan arus mengitari rangkaian. Makin banyak volt, makin kuat dorongannya.`,"Ohm (R)":`Ohm (R)`,"The resistance: he squeezes the pipe, holding the current back. More ohms, a tighter squeeze.":`Hambatan: ia menjepit pipa, menahan arus. Makin banyak ohm, makin erat jepitannya.`,"Amp (A)":`Amp (A)`,"The current: how much gets through. A harder push or a looser squeeze, and more gets through.":`Arus: seberapa banyak yang lewat. Dorongan yang lebih kuat atau jepitan yang lebih longgar, dan lebih banyak yang lewat.`,"The wire, as a pipe":`Kabel, sebagai pipa`,"Current flows along it like water. Its narrow neck is the resistance.":`Arus mengalir di dalamnya seperti air. Lehernya yang sempit adalah hambatannya.`,now:`sekarang`,"AA cell · {0}":`Baterai AA · {0}`,"One cell: {0} and about {1}. The strip on top shows how much is left. Click it to switch the circuit on or off.":`Satu baterai: {0} dan sekitar {1}. Strip di atasnya menunjukkan sisa isinya. Klik untuk menyalakan atau mematikan rangkaian.`,"Click a highlighted part to change it, and switch the power on to see what it does.":`Klik komponen yang disorot untuk mengubahnya, dan nyalakan daya untuk melihat apa yang dilakukannya.`,"Click it to switch on or off":`Klik untuk menyalakan atau mematikan`,"time →":`waktu →`,"time → (last {0})":`waktu → ({0} terakhir)`,"Generator · AC":`Generator · AC`,"Turn the crank and the spinning magnet pushes current one way, then the other: alternating current.":`Putar engkolnya dan magnet yang berputar mendorong arus ke satu arah, lalu ke arah lain: arus bolak-balik.`,"{0} resistor":`Resistor {0}`,"Resists the flow of current: the higher its value, the less current gets through.":`Menghambat aliran arus: makin tinggi nilainya, makin sedikit arus yang lewat.`,"{0} LED":`LED {0}`,"Lights when current flows from the long leg (anode) to the short leg.":`Menyala saat arus mengalir dari kaki panjang (anoda) ke kaki pendek.`,"LED stand":`Dudukan LED`,"Two brass bars: both LEDs stand across them, facing opposite ways.":`Dua batang kuningan: kedua LED berdiri di atasnya, menghadap arah berlawanan.`,"The supply’s voltage over the last moments: flat for DC, a wave for AC.":`Tegangan sumber beberapa saat terakhir: datar untuk DC, gelombang untuk AC.`,"Battery pack · {0} × AA":`Tempat baterai · {0} × AA`,"Two {0} cells in series make {1}. Red lead: +. Black lead: −. Click it to switch it on or off.":`Dua baterai {0} secara seri menjadi {1}. Kabel merah: +. Kabel hitam: −. Klik untuk menyalakan atau mematikannya.`,"Each column of five holes is joined underneath; each power rail is joined along its length.":`Setiap kolom lima lubang tersambung di bawahnya; setiap rel daya tersambung di sepanjangnya.`,"What is joined":`Yang tersambung`,"Holes in one coloured bar are joined by one metal clip inside the board.":`Lubang-lubang dalam satu batang berwarna dihubungkan oleh satu klip logam di dalam papan.`,"Measures volts, amps and ohms. The dial picks what; the sockets take the leads: black always in COM, red in VΩmA (or {0} for big currents).":`Mengukur volt, ampere, dan ohm. Sakelar putar memilih apa yang diukur; soket menerima kabel: hitam selalu di COM, merah di VΩmA (atau {0} untuk arus besar).`,"Is it broken inside? A continuity test tells you: the meter beeps if it conducts.":`Apakah putus di dalam? Uji kontinuitas memberitahumu: alat ukur berbunyi bip jika menghantarkan.`,"Red probe":`Probe merah`,"The red lead: into VΩmA (or {0}), touched to the + side.":`Kabel merah: di VΩmA (atau {0}), ditempelkan ke sisi +.`,"Black probe":`Probe hitam`,"The black lead: always into COM, touched to the − side.":`Kabel hitam: selalu di COM, ditempelkan ke sisi −.`,"A {0} hobby motor: the more current through it, the faster its fan spins.":`Motor hobi {0}: makin besar arus yang melewatinya, makin cepat kipasnya berputar.`,"{0} resistor, {1}":`Resistor {0}, {1}`,POWER:`DAYA`,"Power supply · {0}":`Catu daya · {0}`,"Gives the circuit a steady {0}. Click it to switch the power on or off.":`Memberi rangkaian {0} yang stabil. Klik untuk menyalakan atau mematikan daya.`,"Shows what its two leads measure: volts, ohms or milliamps. Red is +, black is −.":`Menunjukkan apa yang diukur kedua kabelnya: volt, ohm, atau miliampere. Merah adalah +, hitam adalah −.`,"Red lead (+)":`Kabel merah (+)`,"One of the meter’s leads: it measures at the hole it is in.":`Salah satu kabel alat ukur: ia mengukur di lubang tempat ia berada.`,"Black lead (−)":`Kabel hitam (−)`,Brown:`Cokelat`,Black:`Hitam`,Red:`Merah`,Gold:`Emas`,"anything from {0} to {1}":`nilai berapa pun dari {0} sampai {1}`,"Its value is painted on in bands: click one to pick it up, then a paint pot to paint it.":`Nilainya dicat dalam gelang: klik satu untuk mengambilnya, lalu pot cat untuk mengecatnya.`,"1st digit band":`Gelang digit ke-1`,"Click it to pick it up, then click a paint pot.":`Klik untuk mengambilnya, lalu klik pot cat.`,"Click it to pick up its band.":`Klik untuk mengambil gelangnya.`,"2nd digit band":`Gelang digit ke-2`,"Multiplier band":`Gelang pengali`,"Tolerance band":`Gelang toleransi`,"The value":`Nilainya`,"What the bands make: the digits, times the multiplier.":`Yang dihasilkan gelang: digitnya, dikali pengali.`,"Brown paint":`Cat cokelat`,"Click it to paint the band you picked up.":`Klik untuk mengecat gelang yang kamu ambil.`,"Red paint":`Cat merah`,"Orange paint":`Cat oranye`,"Yellow paint":`Cat kuning`,"Green paint":`Cat hijau`,"Blue paint":`Cat biru`,"Violet paint":`Cat ungu`,"Grey paint":`Cat abu-abu`,"White paint":`Cat putih`,"3rd digit band":`Gelang digit ke-3`,"Black paint":`Cat hitam`,"Gold paint":`Cat emas`,"Silver paint":`Cat perak`,Orange:`Oranye`,Yellow:`Kuning`,Green:`Hijau`,Blue:`Biru`,Violet:`Ungu`,Grey:`Abu-abu`,White:`Putih`,Silver:`Perak`,"{0} potentiometer":`Potensiometer {0}`,"Drag around the knob to turn it: the resistance between its middle leg and one end changes from {0} to {1}.":`Seret mengelilingi kenop untuk memutarnya: hambatan antara kaki tengah dan satu ujungnya berubah dari {0} sampai {1}.`,"or drag around the knob":`atau seret mengelilingi kenop`,"Just a wire: it lets through as much current as the circuit will take.":`Hanya kabel: melewatkan arus sebanyak yang diambil rangkaian.`,"A one-way valve for current: it flows towards the black band (the cathode), never back.":`Katup satu arah untuk arus: arus mengalir ke arah gelang hitam (katoda), tidak pernah kembali.`,SUPPLY:`PASOKAN`,"always full = “{0}”":`selalu penuh = “{0}”`,"Tap shut":`Keran tertutup`,"Tap: open":`Buka keran`,"Click a highlighted part to change it, and open the tap to see what it does.":`Klik komponen yang disorot untuk mengubahnya, dan buka keran untuk melihat apa yang dilakukannya.`,"Supply tank · the battery":`Tangki pasokan · baterai`,"Kept full to the same height all the time, like a battery holding its voltage. The height of its water is what pushes the water along.":`Dijaga penuh pada ketinggian yang sama sepanjang waktu, seperti baterai yang mempertahankan tegangannya. Ketinggian airnyalah yang mendorong air mengalir.`,"Tap · the switch":`Keran · sakelar`,"Open it and the water can flow from the supply into the tank, like switching the power on. Click it to open or shut it.":`Buka dan air bisa mengalir dari tangki pasokan ke tangki, seperti menyalakan daya. Klik untuk membuka atau menutupnya.`,"Medium pipe · the resistor":`Pipa sedang · resistor`,"How easily the water gets through: the narrower it is, the more it holds the flow back — like a bigger resistor. Click it to try another.":`Seberapa mudah air lewat: makin sempit, makin kuat menahan aliran — seperti resistor yang lebih besar. Klik untuk mencoba yang lain.`,"Medium tank · the capacitor":`Tangki sedang · kapasitor`,"Fills until its water is as high as the supply’s (the red ring). A wider tank holds more water for the same height — like a bigger capacitance — and takes longer to fill. Click it to try another.":`Terisi sampai airnya setinggi air tangki pasokan (cincin merah). Tangki yang lebih lebar menampung lebih banyak air untuk ketinggian yang sama — seperti kapasitansi yang lebih besar — dan lebih lama terisi. Klik untuk mencoba yang lain.`,"Drain · the push button":`Saluran buang · tombol tekan`,"Hold it open and the tank empties into the tray, like a push button emptying a capacitor.":`Tahan terbuka dan tangki kosong ke nampan, seperti tombol tekan yang mengosongkan kapasitor.`,"Hold to press it":`Tahan untuk menekannya`,"Carries the water from the supply to the tank.":`Membawa air dari tangki pasokan ke tangki.`,"Small tank · the capacitor":`Tangki kecil · kapasitor`,"Large tank · the capacitor":`Tangki besar · kapasitor`,"Narrow pipe · the resistor":`Pipa sempit · resistor`,"Wide pipe · the resistor":`Pipa lebar · resistor`,"Tap open":`Keran terbuka`,"Tap: shut":`Tutup keran`,"Hold it down in the scene":`Tahan di dalam adegan`,"{0} capacitor":`Kapasitor {0}`,"Two plates and a thin insulator, rolled up in a can: it stores charge. The stripe marks the − leg.":`Dua keping dan isolator tipis, digulung dalam kaleng: menyimpan muatan. Garis menandai kaki −.`,"Press and hold it: the two sides connect while it is down.":`Tekan dan tahan: kedua sisi tersambung selama ditekan.`,"AC ADAPTER · {0}":`ADAPTOR AC · {0}`,"AC adapter · {0}":`Adaptor AC · {0}`,"Plugs into the wall and gives {0} of alternating current at its peaks: + then −, {1} times a second. Click it to switch it on or off.":`Dicolokkan ke stopkontak dan memberi {0} arus bolak-balik pada puncaknya: + lalu −, {1} kali per detik. Klik untuk menyalakan atau mematikannya.`,"Gives the circuit {0} of alternating current: it swings from + to − and back, over and over. Click it to switch the power on or off.":`Memberi rangkaian {0} arus bolak-balik: berayun dari + ke − dan kembali, terus-menerus. Klik untuk menyalakan atau mematikan daya.`,"An NPN transistor: a small current into its base (the middle leg) lets a much bigger current flow from its collector to its emitter.":`Transistor NPN: arus kecil yang masuk ke basisnya (kaki tengah) membuat arus yang jauh lebih besar mengalir dari kolektor ke emitornya.`,"Small and not fussy about polarity. Its value is printed as a three-digit code, in picofarads.":`Kecil dan tidak berpolaritas. Nilainya tercetak sebagai kode tiga digit, dalam pikofarad.`,"Push the slider left or right: the middle leg connects to the leg on that side, and stays there.":`Dorong penggeser ke kiri atau kanan: kaki tengah tersambung ke kaki di sisi itu, dan tetap di sana.`,"base current (µA)":`arus basis (µA)`,"collector current (mA)":`arus kolektor (mA)`,"A PNP transistor: a small current out of its base (the middle leg) lets a much bigger current flow from its emitter to its collector.":`Transistor PNP: arus kecil yang keluar dari basisnya (kaki tengah) membuat arus yang jauh lebih besar mengalir dari emitor ke kolektornya.`,"Two copper combs that never quite meet. Put your finger across them and a tiny current flows through your skin.":`Dua sisir tembaga yang tidak pernah benar-benar bertemu. Letakkan jarimu di atasnya dan arus mungil mengalir melalui kulitmu.`,"Hold your finger on it":`Tahan jarimu di atasnya`,"Meter off":`Alat ukur mati`,"Meter: on":`Nyalakan alat ukur`,"Click a highlighted part to change it, and switch the meter on to see what it does.":`Klik komponen yang disorot untuk mengubahnya, dan nyalakan alat ukur untuk melihat apa yang dilakukannya.`,"Its resistance drops as more light falls on it: about {0} in the dark, {1} in bright light.":`Hambatannya turun saat makin banyak cahaya mengenainya: sekitar {0} dalam gelap, {1} dalam cahaya terang.`,"Shines on the light sensor. Click it to make it brighter or dimmer.":`Menyinari sensor cahaya. Klik untuk membuatnya lebih terang atau lebih redup.`,"Meter on":`Alat ukur menyala`,"Meter: off":`Matikan alat ukur`,"{0} thermistor":`Termistor {0}`,"An NTC thermistor: its resistance falls as it warms up. Hold your finger on it to warm it.":`Termistor NTC: hambatannya turun saat menghangat. Tahan jarimu di atasnya untuk menghangatkannya.`,"Two thin iron reeds sealed in glass. A magnet nearby pulls them together and closes the circuit.":`Dua bilah besi tipis yang tersegel dalam kaca. Magnet di dekatnya menarik keduanya dan menutup rangkaian.`,"Click it to bring it up to the reed switch, or take it away again.":`Klik untuk mendekatkannya ke sakelar reed, atau menjauhkannya lagi.`,"{0} trimmer":`Trimpot {0}`,"A small adjustable resistor. Turn its screw to change the resistance between its middle leg and an end one.":`Resistor kecil yang bisa diatur. Putar sekrupnya untuk mengubah hambatan antara kaki tengah dan salah satu kaki ujungnya.`,"A magnet sensor chip with legs for power, ground and its output. A south pole held up to its printed face turns the output on.":`Cip sensor magnet dengan kaki untuk daya, ground, dan keluarannya. Kutub selatan yang dihadapkan ke sisi tercetaknya mengaktifkan keluaran.`,"Click it to move it: away, its south pole to the chip, or its north pole.":`Klik untuk memindahkannya: jauh, kutub selatannya ke cip, atau kutub utaranya.`,Settings:`Pengaturan`,"Callout labels":`Label`,"Cards and pointers around the 3D view":`Kartu dan penunjuk di sekitar tampilan 3D`,"Show the current":`Tampilkan arus`,"Moving dots along the wires while the power is on":`Titik yang bergerak di sepanjang kabel saat daya menyala`,"Floor grid":`Kisi lantai`,"The faint grid under the bench":`Kisi samar di bawah meja kerja`,Turntable:`Putar otomatis`,"Turn a quarter every few seconds when idle":`Berputar seperempat putaran setiap beberapa detik saat diam`,"Reduce motion":`Kurangi gerakan`,"Near-instant transitions":`Transisi hampir seketika`,"Reset progress":`Atur ulang kemajuan`,English:`Inggris`,Spanish:`Spanyol`,Language:`Bahasa`,"Expand sidebar":`Bentangkan bilah samping`,"Collapse sidebar":`Ciutkan bilah samping`,Home:`Beranda`,Lessons:`Pelajaran`,"Designed by":`Didesain oleh`,"Discover <i>·</i> Experiment <i>·</i> Build":`Temukan <i>·</i> Coba <i>·</i> Rakit`,"Interactive 3D workbench. Drag or use WASD to pan, Q and E to rotate, scroll to zoom.":`Meja kerja 3D interaktif. Seret atau pakai WASD untuk menggeser, Q dan E untuk memutar, gulir untuk memperbesar.`,"Part inspector":`Pemeriksa komponen`,Chart:`Grafik`,"Fold the chart":`Lipat grafik`,"Show the chart":`Tampilkan grafik`,"3D view":`Tampilan 3D`,"Drag or WASD to pan · Q / E to rotate · Scroll to zoom":`Seret atau WASD untuk menggeser · Q / E untuk memutar · Gulir untuk memperbesar`,"Turn left (Q)":`Putar ke kiri (Q)`,"Turn left":`Putar ke kiri`,"Turn right (E)":`Putar ke kanan (E)`,"Turn right":`Putar ke kanan`,"Zoom out (−)":`Perkecil (−)`,"Zoom out":`Perkecil`,"Zoom in (+)":`Perbesar (+)`,"Zoom in":`Perbesar`,"Reset view (R)":`Atur ulang tampilan (R)`,"Reset view":`Atur ulang tampilan`,"View from above (T)":`Tampilan dari atas (T)`,"View from above":`Tampilan dari atas`,Progress:`Kemajuan`,"Lesson information":`Informasi pelajaran`,Overview:`Ringkasan`,Maths:`Perhitungan`,"Lesson:":`Pelajaran:`,"Previous lesson":`Pelajaran sebelumnya`,"Previous lesson ([)":`Pelajaran sebelumnya ([)`,"Next lesson":`Pelajaran berikutnya`,"Next lesson (])":`Pelajaran berikutnya (])`,Ready:`Siap`,"Something went wrong while starting. Try reloading the page.":`Terjadi kesalahan saat memulai. Coba muat ulang halaman.`,"3D view unavailable":`Tampilan 3D tidak tersedia`,"The 3D bench is drawn with WebGL, which this browser has turned off. Turn on hardware acceleration in its settings, or try another browser — the lessons and their maths still work.":`Meja kerja 3D digambar dengan WebGL, yang dimatikan oleh browser ini. Nyalakan akselerasi perangkat keras di pengaturannya, atau coba browser lain — pelajaran dan perhitungannya tetap berfungsi.`,"Coming soon":`Segera hadir`,"Coming next:":`Segera hadir:`,Custom:`Kustom`,"✓ That’s {0}!":`✓ Itu {0}!`,Portuguese:`Portugis`,French:`Prancis`,Turkish:`Turki`,Indonesian:`Indonesia`,"Chinese (Simplified)":`Tionghoa (Sederhana)`,"Chinese (Traditional)":`Tionghoa (Tradisional)`,Japanese:`Jepang`,Korean:`Korea`,Arabic:`Arab`,Hebrew:`Ibrani`,Ukrainian:`Ukraina`,German:`Jerman`,Dutch:`Belanda`,Polish:`Polandia`,Vietnamese:`Vietnam`,Russian:`Rusia`,Italian:`Italia`,Greek:`Yunani`,"Current against voltage":`Arus terhadap tegangan`,"Fan speed against resistance":`Kecepatan kipas terhadap hambatan`,"LED current against total resistance":`Arus LED terhadap hambatan total`,"Middle voltage against R2":`Tegangan tengah terhadap R2`,"LED current against the knob":`Arus LED terhadap kenop`,"LED current against supply voltage":`Arus LED terhadap tegangan catu`,"LED current against resistance":`Arus LED terhadap hambatan`,"LED current against lamp brightness":`Arus LED terhadap kecerahan lampu`,"voltage (V)":`tegangan (V)`,"current (mA)":`arus (mA)`,"resistance (Ω)":`hambatan (Ω)`,"fan speed (rpm)":`kecepatan kipas (rpm)`,"total resistance (Ω)":`hambatan total (Ω)`,"LED current (mA)":`arus LED (mA)`,"middle voltage (V)":`tegangan tengah (V)`,"knob (%)":`kenop (%)`,"supply voltage (V)":`tegangan catu (V)`,"lamp brightness (%)":`kecerahan lampu (%)`,"the motor stalls":`motor macet`,"the LED’s limit":`batas LED`,"burnt out":`putus`,"Open the circuit larger":`Buka rangkaian lebih besar`,Diagram:`Diagram`,"Show the circuit as":`Tampilkan rangkaian sebagai`,"Close (Esc)":`Tutup (Esc)`,"This lesson isn’t built on a breadboard.":`Pelajaran ini tidak dirakit di breadboard.`,"Seen from above, as it is built on the breadboard.":`Dilihat dari atas, seperti dirakit di breadboard.`,Zoom:`Zoom`,"Show all of it":`Tampilkan semuanya`,"Drag to resize the chart (double-click: its usual size)":`Seret untuk mengubah ukuran grafik (klik dua kali: ukuran biasanya)`,"Resize the chart":`Ubah ukuran grafik`,"See through the parts":`Komponen tembus pandang`,"+ rail":`rel +`,"− rail":`rel −`,"Where to begin: what makes a circuit, what conducts, how volts, amps and ohms fit together, the kinds of circuit, DC and AC — then how to use a breadboard and a multimeter, and the two rules every circuit keeps.":`Dari mana memulai: apa yang membentuk rangkaian, apa yang menghantar, bagaimana volt, ampere, dan ohm saling terkait, jenis-jenis rangkaian, arus searah dan bolak-balik — lalu cara memakai breadboard dan multimeter, serta dua hukum yang dipatuhi setiap rangkaian.`,"Control how much current flows: eight experiments with a handful of resistors, built with big picture-book parts or on a breadboard.":`Atur seberapa besar arus yang mengalir: delapan percobaan dengan segenggam resistor, dirakit dengan komponen besar ala buku bergambar atau di breadboard.`,"Store charge and let it go again: a water tank to picture it, filling up, holding on, emptying, in series and parallel, smoothing, a timer, reading their values, and two LEDs that flash in turn.":`Menyimpan muatan lalu melepasnya lagi: tangki air untuk membayangkannya, mengisi, menahan, mengosongkan, seri dan paralel, perataan, pewaktu, membaca nilainya, dan dua LED yang berkedip bergantian.`,voltage:`tegangan`,current:`arus`,"V = {0} × sin({1}π × {2} × t)":`V = {0} × sin({1}π × {2} × t)`,"Kirchhoff’s two rules":`Dua hukum Kirchhoff`,"{0}. Kirchhoff’s<br />two rules":`{0}. Dua hukum<br />Kirchhoff`,"Two simple rules hold in every circuit. The current rule: at a junction, all the current that flows in flows out again — none is lost and none is made. The voltage rule: going round any loop, the voltages across the parts add up to the battery’s. Here R1 is in series with R2 and R3 side by side: show the currents, then the voltages, and check both rules.":`Dua hukum sederhana berlaku di setiap rangkaian. Hukum arus: di titik cabang, semua arus yang masuk keluar lagi — tidak ada yang hilang dan tidak ada yang tercipta. Hukum tegangan: mengelilingi loop mana pun, tegangan pada komponen-komponennya berjumlah sama dengan tegangan baterai. Di sini R1 seri dengan R2 dan R3 yang bersebelahan: tampilkan arusnya, lalu tegangannya, dan periksa kedua hukum.`,"Current rule: what flows in, flows out":`Hukum arus: yang masuk, keluar`,"Voltage rule: round a loop they add up":`Hukum tegangan: dalam satu loop, jumlahnya pas`,"Change any resistor: the rules still hold":`Ganti resistor mana pun: hukumnya tetap berlaku`,"All the current<br />flows through it.":`Semua arus<br />melewatinya.`,"One way on from<br />the junction.":`Satu jalan dari<br />titik cabang.`,"The other way:<br />side by side with R2.":`Jalan lainnya:<br />bersebelahan dengan R2.`,Show:`Tampilkan`,Currents:`Arus`,"The current through each resistor: at the junction, I1 = I2 + I3.":`Arus pada setiap resistor: di titik cabang, I1 = I2 + I3.`,Voltages:`Tegangan`,"The voltage across each part: round a loop, V1 + V2 = the battery’s {0}.":`Tegangan pada setiap komponen: dalam satu loop, V1 + V2 = {0} dari baterai.`,"R2 and R3 side by side act like one resistor of {0} × {1} ÷ ({2} + {3}) = {4}, in series with R1, so the battery gives":`R2 dan R3 yang bersebelahan bertindak seperti satu resistor {0} × {1} ÷ ({2} + {3}) = {4}, seri dengan R1, sehingga baterai memberi`,"<b>The current rule.</b> All of I1 reaches the junction after R1, and there it splits, the larger share through the smaller resistor:":`<b>Hukum arus.</b> Seluruh I1 tiba di titik cabang setelah R1, dan di sana terbagi, bagian yang lebih besar melewati resistor yang lebih kecil:`,"<b>The voltage rule.</b> Round the loop through R1 and R2, the parts’ voltages add up to the battery’s; through R1 and R3 too, since R2 and R3 share the same two points:":`<b>Hukum tegangan.</b> Pada loop melalui R1 dan R2, tegangan komponennya berjumlah sama dengan tegangan baterai; melalui R1 dan R3 juga, karena R2 dan R3 berbagi dua titik yang sama:`,"Gustav Kirchhoff wrote them down in {0}, as a student. They are really two things that never fail: charge is never lost or made (the current rule), and the energy the battery gives each bit of charge is all used up on its way round (the voltage rule). With them, any circuit can be worked out, however tangled.":`Gustav Kirchhoff menuliskannya pada {0}, saat masih mahasiswa. Sebenarnya keduanya adalah dua hal yang tak pernah gagal: muatan tak pernah hilang atau tercipta (hukum arus), dan energi yang diberikan baterai ke setiap bagian muatan habis terpakai sepanjang perjalanannya (hukum tegangan). Dengan keduanya, rangkaian apa pun bisa dihitung, serumit apa pun.`,junction:`titik cabang`,"Resistor R3":`Resistor R3`,resistance:`hambatan`,"fan speed":`kecepatan kipas`,"total resistance":`hambatan total`,"LED current":`arus LED`,"middle voltage":`tegangan tengah`,"V2 = V<sub>in</sub> × R2 ÷ (R1 + R2)":`V2 = V<sub>in</sub> × R2 ÷ (R1 + R2)`,knob:`kenop`,"R<sub>pot</sub> = {0}":`R<sub>pot</sub> = {0}`,"Power and heat":`Daya dan panas`,"{0}. Power<br />and heat":`{0}. Daya<br />dan panas`,"Every resistor turns the energy flowing through it into heat. How much each second is its power: the voltage across it times the current through it, P = V × I, in watts. A resistor is rated for how much it can take — a small one a quarter of a watt. Past its rating it overheats, and far past it, it burns out. Switch on and watch it warm up.":`Setiap resistor mengubah energi yang mengalir melewatinya menjadi panas. Banyaknya setiap detik adalah dayanya: tegangan padanya dikali arus yang melewatinya, P = V × I, dalam watt. Sebuah resistor punya rating daya yang sanggup ia tahan — yang kecil seperempat watt. Melewati ratingnya ia kepanasan, dan jauh melewatinya, ia terbakar. Nyalakan dan lihat ia memanas.`,"Power: P = V × I, in watts":`Daya: P = V × I, dalam watt`,"Less resistance: more current, more heat":`Hambatan lebih kecil: arus lebih besar, panas lebih banyak`,"The chart shows it warming up":`Grafik menunjukkan ia memanas`,"Click it to switch<br />on or off.":`Klik untuk menyalakan<br />atau mematikan.`,"Warms as the power<br />flows through it.":`Memanas saat daya<br />mengalir melewatinya.`,Supply:`Catu daya`,"A quarter of the power {0} gives.":`Seperempat daya yang diberikan {0}.`,"The usual supply.":`Catu daya yang biasa.`,"Half as much voltage again: {0} times the power.":`Tegangan setengah kali lebih tinggi: {0} kali dayanya.`,Rating:`Rating daya`,"A small resistor, the usual kind: a quarter of a watt.":`Resistor kecil, jenis yang biasa: seperempat watt.`,"A bigger body, so its heat gets away faster: it takes four times the power.":`Badan yang lebih besar, panasnya lebih cepat keluar: sanggup menahan empat kali daya.`,"Resistor temperature":`Suhu resistor`,"at its rating":`pada rating dayanya`,"it burns":`terbakar`,"All the energy the supply gives the resistor becomes heat. How much each second is its power, in watts:":`Semua energi yang diberikan catu daya ke resistor menjadi panas. Banyaknya setiap detik adalah dayanya, dalam watt:`,"Ohm’s law gives the current, I = {0} ÷ {1} = <b>{2}</b>, so":`Hukum Ohm memberi arusnya, I = {0} ÷ {1} = <b>{2}</b>, jadi`,"The two together make P = V² ÷ R: half the resistance gives twice the power, and twice the voltage four times as much.":`Keduanya bersama menjadi P = V² ÷ R: setengah hambatan memberi dua kali daya, dan dua kali tegangan empat kali lebih banyak.`,Power:`Daya`,"A ¼ W one":`Yang ¼ W`,"hot, within its rating":`panas, masih dalam rating dayanya`,"warm, well within its rating":`hangat, jauh di bawah rating dayanya`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A ¼ W resistor warms about {0} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{1}</b>: hot, within its rating.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor ¼ W memanas sekitar {0} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{1}</b>: panas, masih dalam rating dayanya.`,"At its rating a resistor runs hot enough to burn a finger, so designers keep it at half its rating or less. Big resistors are rated for more because their bigger body loses heat faster. Heat is also why a phone charger, or a light bulb, warms up: some of the power they use always ends up as heat.":`Pada rating dayanya, resistor cukup panas untuk membakar jari, jadi para perancang memakainya pada setengah rating atau kurang. Resistor besar punya rating lebih tinggi karena badannya yang lebih besar melepas panas lebih cepat. Panas juga yang membuat pengisi daya ponsel, atau bohlam, menjadi hangat: sebagian daya yang mereka pakai selalu berakhir menjadi panas.`,"{0}, rated ¼ W":`{0}, rating ¼ W`,"A {0} one":`Yang {0}`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A {0} resistor warms about {1} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{2}</b>: warm, well within its rating.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor {0} memanas sekitar {1} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{2}</b>: hangat, jauh di bawah rating dayanya.`,"{0}, rated {1}":`{0}, rating {1}`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A ¼ W resistor warms about {0} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{1}</b>: warm, well within its rating.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor ¼ W memanas sekitar {0} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{1}</b>: hangat, jauh di bawah rating dayanya.`,"burns out":`terbakar`,"too hot: over its rating":`terlalu panas: melebihi rating dayanya`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A ¼ W resistor warms about {0} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{1}</b>: burns out.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor ¼ W memanas sekitar {0} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{1}</b>: terbakar.`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A {0} resistor warms about {1} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{2}</b>: hot, within its rating.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor {0} memanas sekitar {1} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{2}</b>: panas, masih dalam rating dayanya.`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A ¼ W resistor warms about {0} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{1}</b>: too hot: over its rating.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor ¼ W memanas sekitar {0} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{1}</b>: terlalu panas, melebihi rating dayanya.`,"The heat has to get out into the air. A {0} resistor warms about {1} for every watt, so this one settles near <b>{2}</b>: too hot: over its rating.":`Panasnya harus keluar ke udara. Resistor {0} memanas sekitar {1} untuk setiap watt, jadi yang ini mantap di dekat <b>{2}</b>: terlalu panas, melebihi rating dayanya.`,"Wheatstone bridge":`Jembatan Wheatstone`,"{0}. Wheatstone<br />bridge":`{0}. Jembatan<br />Wheatstone`,"Measure a resistor: the Wheatstone bridge":`Mengukur resistor: jembatan Wheatstone`,"Two voltage dividers side by side, and a meter between their middles. On the left, two equal resistors hold their middle at exactly half the supply. On the right, a pot sits over a mystery resistor. Turn the knob until the meter reads zero: then the pot’s resistance equals the mystery one’s, whatever the battery gives.":`Dua pembagi tegangan bersebelahan, dan alat ukur di antara titik tengahnya. Di kiri, dua resistor yang sama menahan titik tengahnya tepat di setengah tegangan catu daya. Di kanan, sebuah potensiometer berada di atas resistor misteri. Putar kenop sampai alat ukur menunjukkan nol: saat itu hambatan potensiometer sama dengan hambatan resistor misteri, berapa pun tegangan baterainya.`,"Two dividers, a meter between their middles":`Dua pembagi, alat ukur di antara titik tengahnya`,"Turn the knob until the meter reads {0}":`Putar kenop sampai alat ukur menunjukkan {0}`,"Then the pot equals the mystery resistor":`Saat itu potensiometer sama dengan resistor misteri`,"R3 · Pot":`R3 · Potensiometer`,"Turn it until the<br />meter reads {0}.":`Putar sampai alat<br />ukur menunjukkan {0}.`,Mystery:`Misteri`,"The resistor to<br />be measured.":`Resistor yang<br />akan diukur.`,"Half of the left<br />divider.":`Setengah dari<br />pembagi kiri.`,"The other half:<br />equal to R1.":`Setengah lainnya:<br />sama dengan R1.`,"Between the two<br />middles.":`Di antara kedua<br />titik tengah.`,"Where R1 meets R2.":`Tempat R1 bertemu R2.`,"Where R3 meets Rx.":`Tempat R3 bertemu Rx.`,"Knob (R3)":`Kenop (R3)`,"Mystery resistor":`Resistor misteri`,"Mystery A":`Misteri A`,"Find its value: turn the knob until the meter reads {0}.":`Cari nilainya: putar kenop sampai alat ukur menunjukkan {0}.`,"Mystery B":`Misteri B`,"Mystery C":`Misteri C`,"Meter against the knob":`Alat ukur terhadap kenop`,balanced:`seimbang`,meter:`alat ukur`,"Each side is a voltage divider. On the left, two equal resistors put their middle, A, at half the supply:":`Setiap sisi adalah pembagi tegangan. Di kiri, dua resistor yang sama menempatkan titik tengahnya, A, di setengah tegangan catu daya:`,"On the right, the pot (R3, now {0}) sits over the mystery resistor Rx, so B is at":`Di kanan, potensiometer (R3, sekarang {0}) berada di atas resistor misteri Rx, jadi B berada di`,"The meter, black probe on A and red on B, reads the difference, V<sub>B</sub> − V<sub>A</sub> = <b>{0}</b>. It is zero — the bridge is <i>balanced</i> — when both sides divide the same way:":`Alat ukur, probe hitam di A dan merah di B, membaca selisihnya, V<sub>B</sub> − V<sub>A</sub> = <b>{0}</b>. Selisihnya nol — jembatannya <i>seimbang</i> — saat kedua sisi membagi dengan cara yang sama:`,"With R1 = R2 that means R3 = Rx. Not yet: turn the knob up — B is above A, so R3 needs to be bigger.":`Dengan R1 = R2, artinya R3 = Rx. Belum: putar kenop ke atas — B di atas A, jadi R3 perlu lebih besar.`,"The trick is that the zero doesn’t depend on the battery’s voltage, or on how accurate the meter is: it only has to show when nothing is there. That makes bridges very precise, and they still measure tiny changes in resistance: strain gauges in scales, and sensors for temperature and pressure.":`Kuncinya, nol itu tidak bergantung pada tegangan baterai, atau seberapa akurat alat ukurnya: alat ukur hanya perlu menunjukkan saat tidak ada apa-apa. Itu membuat jembatan sangat presisi, dan sampai sekarang dipakai mengukur perubahan hambatan yang sangat kecil: strain gauge di timbangan, dan sensor suhu dan tekanan.`,"Resistors R1 and R2":`Resistor R1 dan R2`,"{0} each":`masing-masing {0}`,"Potentiometer R3":`Potensiometer R3`,"Mystery resistor A":`Resistor misteri A`,"to be measured":`yang akan diukur`,"set to V, between the two middles":`pada V, di antara kedua titik tengah`,"Mystery resistor B":`Resistor misteri B`,"Mystery resistor C":`Resistor misteri C`,"With R1 = R2 that means R3 = Rx. {t0}Balanced: the mystery resistor is {0}.</b>":`Dengan R1 = R2, artinya R3 = Rx. {t0}Seimbang: resistor misterinya {0}.</b>`,"balanced · {0}":`seimbang · {0}`,"With R1 = R2 that means R3 = Rx. Not yet: turn the knob down — B is below A, so R3 needs to be smaller.":`Dengan R1 = R2, artinya R3 = Rx. Belum: putar kenop ke bawah — B di bawah A, jadi R3 perlu lebih kecil.`,"supply voltage":`tegangan catu daya`,"Two flashing LEDs":`Dua LED berkedip`,"{0}. Two flashing<br />LEDs":`{0}. Dua LED<br />berkedip`,"Two flashing LEDs: the astable":`Dua LED berkedip: rangkaian astabil`,"With two transistors and two capacitors, two LEDs take turns on their own for as long as the power is on. While one transistor is on, the other’s base slowly climbs back up through its {0} as a capacitor charges; at {1} it switches on, and its capacitor kicks the first one off. Bigger capacitors, slower flashing — and each capacitor sets how long one LED stays lit.":`Dengan dua transistor dan dua kapasitor, dua LED menyala bergantian sendiri selama dayanya menyala. Selama satu transistor aktif, basis transistor yang lain perlahan naik lagi melalui {0}-nya sementara sebuah kapasitor terisi; saat mencapai {1} ia aktif, dan kapasitornya langsung mematikan yang pertama. Kapasitor lebih besar, kedipan lebih lambat — dan setiap kapasitor menentukan berapa lama satu LED tetap menyala.`,"Two transistors switching each other":`Dua transistor yang saling menyalakan`,"Each capacitor sets one LED’s time":`Setiap kapasitor menentukan waktu satu LED`,"The chart shows both bases climbing to {0}":`Grafik menunjukkan kedua basis naik ke {0}`,"On while the red<br />LED is lit.":`Aktif selama LED<br />merah menyala.`,"On while the green<br />LED is lit.":`Aktif selama LED<br />hijau menyala.`,"Sets how long the<br />red LED stays on.":`Menentukan berapa lama<br />LED merah menyala.`,"Sets the green<br />LED’s time.":`Menentukan waktu<br />LED hijau.`,"C1 (the red LED’s time)":`C1 (waktu LED merah)`,"The red LED stays on about {0} each time.":`LED merah menyala sekitar {0} setiap kali.`,"C2 (the green LED’s time)":`C2 (waktu LED hijau)`,"The green LED stays on about {0} each time.":`LED hijau menyala sekitar {0} setiap kali.`,"Q1’s base (dashed: Q2’s)":`Basis Q1 (putus-putus: basis Q2)`,"switches on at {0}":`aktif pada {0}`,"While Q1 is on, its collector sits at {0}, and C1 holds Q2’s base below {1} — about {2} just after the swap. Q2 stays off until its base has climbed back to {3}, as C1 charges through Q2’s {4}. How long that takes is set by the two together:":`Selama Q1 aktif, kolektornya berada di {0}, dan C1 menahan basis Q2 di bawah {1} — sekitar {2} tepat setelah pergantian. Q2 tetap mati sampai basisnya naik lagi ke {3}, sementara C1 terisi melalui {4} milik Q2. Berapa lama itu ditentukan oleh keduanya bersama:`,"The base heads for {0} but only has to get from {1} to {2}, which takes about {3} τ: the red LED stays on for <b>{4}</b>. Then Q2 switches on, and through C2 its falling collector pulls Q1’s base down in turn: the green LED is on for":`Basisnya menuju {0} tetapi hanya perlu naik dari {1} ke {2}, yang memakan sekitar {3} τ: LED merah menyala selama <b>{4}</b>. Lalu Q2 aktif, dan lewat C2 kolektornya yang turun ganti menarik basis Q1 ke bawah: LED hijau menyala selama`,"One whole flash of each takes {0}: {1} times a second.":`Satu kedipan penuh masing-masing memakan {0}: {1} kali per detik.`,"Switch the power on to start it.":`Nyalakan dayanya untuk memulai.`,"You will see it said that each half lasts {0} × R × C. That holds for a higher supply, with plain resistors as the loads; here, with LEDs in the way, the collectors swing only about a volt, so the bases are pulled down less far and the halves are shorter. The red LED needs less voltage than the green, so its side swings a little further, and with equal capacitors the red stays on a little longer. Circuits like this one — astable, never resting in one state — keep time in flashers and in buzzers that beep, and were how early computers made their clock.":`Kamu akan menemukan bahwa setiap setengah siklus berlangsung {0} × R × C. Itu berlaku untuk catu daya yang lebih tinggi dengan resistor biasa sebagai bebannya; di sini, dengan LED di jalurnya, kolektor hanya berayun sekitar satu volt, jadi basis tertarik ke bawah tidak sejauh itu dan setengah siklusnya lebih pendek. LED merah butuh tegangan lebih kecil daripada yang hijau, jadi sisinya berayun sedikit lebih jauh, dan dengan kapasitor yang sama yang merah menyala sedikit lebih lama. Rangkaian seperti ini — astabil, tak pernah diam di satu keadaan — menjaga waktu di lampu kedip dan buzzer yang berbunyi bip, dan dulu menjadi detak jam komputer-komputer pertama.`,"{0} · to each base, {1} · for each LED":`{0} · ke setiap basis, {1} · untuk setiap LED`,LEDs:`LED`,"red and green":`merah dan hijau`,"{t0}Now: Q1 on, the red LED lit.</b>":`{t0}Sekarang: Q1 aktif, LED merah menyala.</b>`,"{t0}Now: Q2 on, the green LED lit.</b>":`{t0}Sekarang: Q2 aktif, LED hijau menyala.</b>`,"{0} · right and left":`{0} · kanan dan kiri`,"lamp brightness":`kecerahan lampu`,"NTC {0}":`NTC {0}`,"R<sub>top</sub> = {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>":`R<sub>atas</sub> = {0} + {1} = <b>{2}</b>`,"R<sub>LDR</sub> = {0} × {1} ÷ {2} = <b>{3}</b>":`R<sub>LDR</sub> = {0} × {1} ÷ {2} = <b>{3}</b>`,Hall:`Hall`,GND:`GND`,OUT:`OUT`,"{0} resistor, ¼ W":`Resistor {0}, ¼ W`,"Jumper wire":`Kabel jumper`,"meter (V)":`alat ukur (V)`,"Point A":`Titik A`,"Where R1 meets R2: the middle of the left divider, always at half the supply. The meter’s black lead is clamped here.":`Tempat R1 bertemu R2: titik tengah pembagi kiri, selalu di setengah tegangan catu daya. Kabel hitam alat ukur dijepit di sini.`,"Point B":`Titik B`,"Where the pot meets the mystery resistor: the middle of the right divider. The meter’s red lead is clamped here.":`Tempat potensiometer bertemu resistor misteri: titik tengah pembagi kanan. Kabel merah alat ukur dijepit di sini.`,"Carries a signal or power between two points.":`Menyalurkan sinyal atau daya antara dua titik.`};export{e as default};